t["subzone:dormitory"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,240,14.610.0,21.331.0,48.302.0,42.294.0,30.221.0,52.202.0",["h"]="08316c",["n"]="Dormitorio",["s"]="Dormitorio. Dormitorio es un sector residencial dentro de la caída capital tecnológica de Gnomeregan. Antaño proporcionaba alojamiento a innumerables ciudadanos gnomos, pero ahora se encuentra asfixiado por la lluvia radiactiva y plagado de salvajes troggs irradiados. Ubicado justo después de las cámaras de descontaminación de la Zona Limpia, Dormitorio albergaba antiguamente a los inventores, obreros y familias de Gnomeregan. Cuando el Manitas Mayor Mekkatorque inició la purga de radiación de emergencia para combatir a la horda invasora de troggs, este sector densamente poblado se convirtió en una trampa. En la actualidad, sus salas comunales y unidades residenciales están completamente desprovistas de vida gnómica, ocupadas en su lugar por troggs mutados que prosperan en el miasma radiactivo. Los viajeros que descienden hacia los niveles inferiores de la ciudad deben luchar a través de este trágico recordatorio de la catástrofe para alcanzar la parte inferior de la Sala de los Engranajes.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="Even amid total bio-containment failure, automated terminals like the Matrix Punchograph 3005-B continue processing algorithmic security punch cards flawlessly.",["race:Gnome"]="Stepping into the Dormitory is personal for every gnome: this was once your home, now reduced to irradiated rubble and overrun by the very brutes who drove you from it."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Dormitory served as everyday living quarters for Gnomeregan's vast population of inventors, workers, and their families. Its proximity to industrial and civic sectors allowed gnome citizens easy access between their workstations and resting bunks before toxic radiation flooded the lower corridors.",["al"]={"what is dormitory","dormitory purpose","who lived here"},["q"]="What was the Dormitory used for before the fall?"},{["a"]="When the troggs breached the city from beneath, High Tinker Mekkatorque flooded the city with toxic gas to kill them. Instead of wiping them out, the radiation mutated the surviving troggs, making them more vicious and entirely resistant to the irradiated environment of the residential blocks.",["al"]={"why troggs here","trogg infestation dormitory","irradiated troggs"},["q"]="Why is the Dormitory infested with troggs?"},{["a"]="The Dormitory sits just beyond the sanitized airlocks of the Clean Zone and connects the upper levels to the lower level of the Hall of Gears, making it an unavoidable chokepoint for anyone pushing deeper into Gnomeregan.",["al"]={"dormitory exits","where to go from dormitory","dormitory connections"},["q"]="Where does the Dormitory lead?"},{["a"]="The Matrix Punchograph 3005-B terminals process security punch cards. Their encoded cards grant clearance to higher-security terminals, allowing the recovery of important data left behind in Gnomeregan.",["al"]={"punchograph","matrix punchograph 3005-B","punch cards"},["q"]="What are the Matrix Punchograph machines found here?"}},["kw"]={"clean zone","dormitory","gnomeregan","hall of gears","punchograph","trogg"},["n"]="Dormitory",["s"]="The Dormitory is a residential sector within the fallen technological capital of Gnomeregan. Once providing living quarters for countless gnome citizens, it now lies choked with radioactive fallout and crawls with savage, irradiated troggs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated just past the decontamination chambers of the Clean Zone, the Dormitory formerly housed the inventors, laborers, and families of Gnomeregan. When High Tinker Mekkatorque initiated the emergency radiation venting to combat the invading trogg horde, this densely populated sector became a trap. Today, its communal halls and living units are completely abandoned by gnomish life, occupied instead by mutated troggs that thrive in the radioactive miasma. Travelers descending toward the lower levels of the city must fight through this tragic reminder of the catastrophe to reach the lower Hall of Gears.",["t"]="A Home Overrun"},{["b"]="Amid the abandoned living quarters, remnants of the city's administrative apparatus still function. The Matrix Punchograph 3005-B machines process security punch cards. These terminals provide clearance for higher-security data terminals deeper within Gnomeregan, helping recover important records left behind when the gnomes fled.",["t"]="Punchograph Terminals"}}}}}
t["subzone:drag"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="4,367,26.607.0,33.442.0,39.260.0,25.291.0,12.177.0,48.213.0",["h"]="29cc22",["n"]="Calle Mayor",["s"]="Calle Mayor. La Calle Mayor es una bulliciosa y sombría vía tallada en la roca roja de Orgrimmar, que une el Valle de la Fuerza con el Valle del Honor y el Valle de la Sabiduría. Conocida en todo Durotar como el corazón del comercio de la capital, las paredes de su cañón están repletas de artesanos, comerciantes y artífices. También oculta el descenso cavernoso hacia el infame Circo de las Sombras. Enclavada en las profundidades de los muros rojos del cañón de Orgrimmar, La Calle Mayor sirve como la columna vertebral comercial de la capital de la Horda. Mientras que el Valle de la Fuerza se centra en la concentración militar y el mando administrativo, en La Calle Mayor es donde se desarrolla la vida diaria de la ciudad. A la sombra de altos riscos y pieles, la calle está impregnada de los olores de las cubas de curtido, los calderos de alquimia burbujeantes y el traqueteo de los engranajes de los manitas. Artesanos de casi todas las disciplinas se reúnen aquí para ejercer sus oficios y enseñar a los aspirantes a aventureros, desde peletería y sastrería hasta talleres de ingeniería goblin, como el Taller de Nogg.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Every traveler passing through the capital eventually treads the Drag, as it links Orgrimmar's martial core directly to the communal and mystical quarters.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Drag is home to Nogg's Machine Shop, where goblin tinkerers impart schematics, explosives, and specialized engineering knowledge to the Horde."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Drag is Orgrimmar's primary shopping and trade district. It hosts trainers and supply vendors for a wide array of professions, including alchemy, tailoring, leatherworking, skinning, enchanting, and engineering, alongside general salvage and trading goods.",["al"]={"purpose of the drag","what is the drag","what shops are in the drag"},["q"]="What is the Drag used for in Orgrimmar?"},{["a"]="The canyon street links the Valley of Strength in the south to the Valley of Honor in the northeast, with pathways also leading toward the Valley of Wisdom. Crucially, the entrance descending into the shadowy caverns of the Cleft of Shadow is located along the western cliffside of the Drag.",["al"]={"drag connections","how to get to cleft of shadow","where does the drag go"},["q"]="Where does the Drag lead?"},{["a"]="Nogg is an enterprising goblin engineer who operates Nogg's Machine Shop along the Drag, serving as a prominent engineering trainer and gadget supplier for members of the Horde.",["al"]={"noggs machine shop","who runs the machine shop"},["q"]="Who is Nogg?"},{["a"]="Most crafting and gathering professions maintain shops along the lower and upper shelves of the Drag, but not all of them. Notably, the city's blacksmiths and miners prefer the fiery forges of the Valley of Honor.",["al"]={"where are trainers in orgrimmar","first aid trainer drag"},["q"]="Are all profession trainers located in the Drag?"}},["kw"]={"alchemy","cleft of shadow","drag","leatherworking","nogg","orgrimmar","salvage","tailoring","the drag"},["n"]="Drag",["s"]="The Drag is a bustling, shaded thoroughfare carved into the red rock of Orgrimmar, linking the Valley of Strength to the Valley of Honor and the Valley of Wisdom. Known throughout Durotar as the heart of the capital's commerce, its canyon walls are lined with crafters, traders, and artisans. It also conceals the cavernous descent into the notorious Cleft of Shadow.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked deep between the red canyon walls of Orgrimmar, the Drag serves as the commercial backbone of the Horde's capital. While the Valley of Strength focuses on military muster and administrative command, the Drag is where daily city life unfolds. Shaded under high cliffs and hides, the street is thick with the smells of tanning vats, bubbling alchemical cauldrons, and the clatter of tinkerers' gears. Craftsmen of almost every discipline gather here to practice their trades and teach aspiring adventurers, from leatherworking and tailoring to goblin-led engineering workshops like Nogg's Machine Shop.",["t"]="The Artisan's Thoroughfare"},{["b"]="Beyond housing merchant storefronts and salvage houses, the Drag occupies an uneasy position within Orgrimmar's social geography. Nestled along its canyon face lies the guarded entrance to the subterranean Cleft of Shadow. This makes the Drag an inescapable crossroads where honest tradesmen, shaman on their way to the Valley of Wisdom, and secretive practitioners of dark arts brush shoulders beneath the dim, dusty overhangs of the canyon.",["t"]="A Crossroads of Shadows and Craft"}}}}}
t["subzone:dreadmist-den"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,246,23.449.0,14.425.1,22.180.0,40.187.0,36.165.0,40.244.0",["h"]="d80150",["n"]="Cubil Calígine",["s"]="Cubil Calígine. El Cubil Calígine es una caverna subterránea excavada bajo los riscos de Cima Calígine, en el norte de Los Baldíos. Controlada por la secta Filo Ardiente, la caverna está perpetuamente envuelta en una inquietante bruma roja y sirve como santuario para la adoración de demonios. El Cubil Calígine se encuentra oculto entre las escarpadas laderas de Cima Calígine y sirve como un oscuro santuario para los sectarios de Filo Ardiente. En su interior, el aire es denso debido a un espeso vapor carmesí que envuelve la caverna en una penumbra inquietante. Lejos de la atenta mirada de la Horda en las llanuras inferiores, la secta celebra viles ritos demoníacos en estos túneles de piedra, custodiando sus reliquias blasfemas y conspirando para extender su corrupción por todo Kalimdor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="The demonic relics and volatile fel energies cultivated within Dreadmist Den draw the keen interest of warlocks looking to exploit the Burning Blade's dark secrets.",["faction:Horde"]="The presence of a Burning Blade den overlooking the Barrens is an intolerable danger to nearby trade routes and settlements, demanding swift action from Horde defenders."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dreadmist Den is a cave system hidden within Dreadmist Peak in the northern Barrens. It serves as an active enclave and ritual ground for members of the shadowy Burning Blade cult.",["al"]={"dreadmist den","what is dreadmist den","barrens dreadmist cave"},["q"]="What is Dreadmist Den?"},{["a"]="The unnatural crimson vapor is a product of demonic sorcery permeating the peak. It cloaks the cavern in twilight and is tied to the dark artifacts and rituals maintained by the cultists.",["al"]={"red haze dreadmist","crimson fog barrens","red mist dreadmist den"},["q"]="What causes the red mist inside the den?"},{["a"]="The Demon Seed is a dark artifact kept deep within Dreadmist Den. It holds immense value to the Burning Blade cultists, acting as a potent focus for their fel magic.",["al"]={"demon seed","what is demon seed","artifact in dreadmist den"},["q"]="What is the Demon Seed found inside?"},{["a"]="The Burning Blade cult openly worships demons and seeks to undermine the Horde from within Kalimdor. Leaving a stronghold of demon-worshipping cultists so close to Crossroads and Orgrimmar poses a constant threat to the security of the Barrens.",["al"]={"horde dreadmist den","why clear dreadmist den","orcs burning blade barrens"},["q"]="Why does the Horde care about this cave?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","burning blade","cultists","demon seed","dreadmist den","dreadmist peak","red mist"},["n"]="Dreadmist Den",["s"]="Dreadmist Den is a subterranean cavern carved beneath the crags of Dreadmist Peak in the northern Barrens. Controlled by the Burning Blade cult, the cavern is perpetually smothered in an unnerving red haze and serves as a shrine to demon worship.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Dreadmist Den lies tucked within the jagged slopes of Dreadmist Peak, serving as a dark sanctuary for the Burning Blade cultists. Inside, the air hangs heavy with a thick, crimson vapor that blankets the cavern in an eerie twilight. Far from the watchful eyes of the Horde in the plains below, the cult conducts foul demonic rites within these stone tunnels, guarding their blasphemous relics and plotting to spread their corruption across Kalimdor.",["t"]="A Den of Wicked Shadows"},{["b"]="At the deepest heart of the cavern rests the Demon Seed, a prized artifact of fel power cherished by the cultists. It acts as an anchor of demonic taint within the region, sustaining the dark haze that clings to the cavern walls. For Horde scouts and aspiring warlocks tracking the Burning Blade's machinations, plunging into this den is a dangerous necessity to uncover the full reach of demonic infiltration in the Barrens.",["t"]="The Demon Seed"}}}}}
t["subzone:dreadmist-peak"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,224,19.572.0,24.503.1,51.189.0,28.206.0,51.266.0,32.195.0",["h"]="610712",["n"]="Cima Calígine",["s"]="Cima Calígine. Cima Calígine es una montaña escarpada y desolada que se alza al noroeste de El Cruce, en Los Baldíos. Envuelto en un miasma carmesí sobrenatural, el pico sirve como reducto aislado para los cultistas demoníacos del Filo Ardiente. Elevándose muy por encima de las áridas sabanas de Los Baldíos, Cima Calígine destaca como un lugar de maldad palpable. A medida que los viajeros ascienden por los riscos, el cielo brillante queda oculto por una densa neblina rojiza: el miasma residual de una antigua maldición demoníaca. En la cresta de la montaña y dentro de sus cavidades subterráneas, el culto del Filo Ardiente opera en secreto, albergando a brujos, toxicólogos y diabólicos grellkin. Desde esta posición privilegiada, los cultistas propagan venenos en el nivel freático cercano y conspiran contra los incipientes poderes que se asientan en el centro de Kalimdor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Tauren druids from Camp Taurajo investigate Dreadmist Peak's water sources, seeking to identify the unnatural toxins poisoning the gazelles and wildlife of the plains.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance agents operating near Ashenvale trace corrupting magic bound to befouled water elementals straight to Sarilus Foulborne, an undead summoner lurking on the peak."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The reddish-orange fog smothering the peak is lingering miasma left behind by an ancient demonic curse, sustained and intensified by the foul rituals of the resident Burning Blade warlocks.",["al"]={"red mist dreadmist","orange fog dreadmist peak","why is dreadmist red"},["q"]="Why is the air red and foggy around Dreadmist Peak?"},{["a"]="The mountain is controlled by the Burning Blade cult, who keep watch along its trails and guard Dreadmist Den beneath. It is also occupied by dark figures such as the renegade undead mage Sarilus Foulborne.",["al"]={"who lives on dreadmist peak","dreadmist peak enemies","burning blade dreadmist"},["q"]="Who controls Dreadmist Peak?"},{["a"]="Three years after the Third War, a minor demon named Zmodlor used Dreadmist Peak as a base to orchestrate hostilities between the Horde and Theramore. Lady Jaina Proudmoore, accompanied by Aegwynn, tracked the plot here and banished the demon, narrowly averting war.",["al"]={"jaina dreadmist peak","zmodlor dreadmist","theramore war barrens"},["q"]="What happened here between Theramore and the Horde?"},{["a"]="Follow the main road north from the Crossroads until it forks toward Ashenvale and Stonetalon. Face northwest to see the crag looming overhead, then ascend the spiraling path up its eastern face.",["al"]={"getting to dreadmist peak","dreadmist peak location","dreadmist path"},["q"]="How do you reach Dreadmist Peak?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","burning blade","dreadmist den","dreadmist peak","jaina proudmoore","miasma","sarilus foulborne","zmodlor"},["n"]="Dreadmist Peak",["s"]="Dreadmist Peak is a jagged, desolate mountain looming northwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. Shrouded in an unnatural, crimson miasma, the peak serves as a secluded redoubt for the demonic cultists of the Burning Blade.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Rising high above the arid savannas of the Barrens, Dreadmist Peak stands out as a site of palpable evil. As travelers wind their way up the crags, the bright sky is blotted out by a dense, reddish haze—the residual miasma of an ancient demonic curse. At the mountain's crest and within its subterranean hollows, the Burning Blade cult operates in secret, harboring warlocks, toxicologists, and fiendish grellkin. From this vantage, the cultists spread poisons into the nearby water table and scheme against the nascent powers establishing control over central Kalimdor.",["t"]="A Den of Corruption"},{["b"]="Beyond housing warlocks and their dark rituals around Dreadmist Den, the peak has drawn other malevolent figures. The rogue Forsaken mage Sarilus Foulborne made his camp upon the heights, bending elemental forces to corrupt water spirits as far north as Ashenvale. Furthermore, when the minor demon Zmodlor conspired to spark outright war between Thrall's Horde and Theramore, it was here that Lady Jaina Proudmoore and Aegwynn confronted and banished the entity, cutting short a catastrophic bloodbath.",["t"]="A Convergence of Schemes"}}}}}
t["subzone:dry-hills"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,319,25.579.0,24.388.0,48.194.0,27.189.0,41.214.0,68.190.0",["h"]="6f793e",["n"]="Las Colinas Áridas",["s"]="Las Colinas Áridas. Las Colinas Áridas forman el escarpado rincón noroccidental de los Baldíos, ubicado al pie de las estribaciones de Sierra Espolón. Al contrario de lo que sugiere su nombre, estas tierras altas son notablemente más verdes que las áridas llanuras situadas más abajo, aunque son notoriamente peligrosas debido a las agresivas arpías Alabruja que anidan en sus riscos. Escondidas donde las áridas llanuras se elevan hacia Sierra Espolón, Las Colinas Áridas son en cierto modo un nombre poco apropiado, pues cuentan con mucha más vegetación y matorrales que las sabanas blanqueadas por el sol del sur. Aun así, esta exuberante región al pie de las colinas ofrece poca seguridad a los viajeros. Los riscos están dominados por las arpías Alabruja, lideradas por la matriarca Serena Sangrepluma. Desde estas alturas, sus partidas de asalto bajan en picado para atacar a las caravanas de suministros que transitan por el tramo norte del Camino del Oro, dejando fortificaciones orcas abandonadas y máquinas de asedio deterioradas pudriéndose entre la maleza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The rugged uplands offer rich hunting grounds filled with swift Hecklefang hyenas, predatory Sunscale scytheclaws, and fierce harpies.",["faction:Horde"]="The Witchwing harpies nesting in the Dry Hills pose a constant danger to the northern trade arteries linking the Crossroads to Stonetalon and Ashenvale, demanding regular culling from Horde champions."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Despite the moniker, the hills receive runoff and cooler air from the adjacent Stonetalon range, making them significantly greener than the arid plains stretching across the rest of the Barrens.",["al"]={"why called dry hills","dry hills green","dry hills terrain"},["q"]="Why is it called the Dry Hills if it's so green?"},{["a"]="The hills are controlled almost entirely by the Witchwing tribe of harpies, ruled by Serena Bloodfeather. Wild beasts like Hecklefang hyenas and Sunscale raptors also roam the rocky slopes.",["al"]={"who is in dry hills","dry hills inhabitants","harpies dry hills"},["q"]="Who lives in the Dry Hills?"},{["a"]="Witchwing raiders frequently descend from the hills to plunder supply caravans traveling along the northern Gold Road, prompting Horde commanders to issue bounties to cull their numbers and eliminate their leaders.",["al"]={"horde dry hills","why fight harpies here","dry hills quests"},["q"]="Why is the Horde interested in this area?"},{["a"]="They are remnants of an abandoned orcish outpost, likely established to watch the mountain passes or secure the northern routes before being overwhelmed or abandoned to the roosting harpies.",["al"]={"orc tower dry hills","abandoned catapults dry hills","orc ruins dry hills"},["q"]="What are the ruined towers and catapults in the middle of the hills?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","dry hills","gold road","harpies","serena bloodfeather","stonetalon","witchwing"},["n"]="Dry Hills",["s"]="The Dry Hills form the rugged northwestern corner of the Barrens, nestled against the foothills of the Stonetalon Mountains. Contrary to their name, these uplands are noticeably greener than the arid plains below, though they are notoriously dangerous due to the aggressive Witchwing harpies roosting along their crags.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away where the arid plains rise toward the Stonetalon Mountains, the Dry Hills are somewhat of a misnomer, possessing far more verdant brush and shrubbery than the sun-bleached savannas to the south. Yet this lush foothill region offers little safety for travelers. The bluffs are dominated by the Witchwing harpies, led by the matriarch Serena Bloodfeather. From these heights, their raiding parties sweep down to prey on supply caravans using the northern stretch of the Gold Road, leaving abandoned orcish fortifications and derelict siege engines rotting in the brush.",["t"]="A Green Haven for Harpies"},{["b"]="Because the Witchwing harpies routinely strike out of the hills to bleed trade routes and harass nearby settlements, the Horde maintains a standing bounty on their feathers. Adventurers venturing deep into the rocky ravines will encounter not only heavily defended harpy nests and roosts, but also prowling Hecklefang hyenas and fierce Sunscale raptors that hunt throughout the highlands.",["t"]="Threat to the Crossroads"}}}}}
t["subzone:drygulch-ravine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,284,31.536.0,25.467.0,36.152.0,39.141.0,42.189.0,43.203.0",["h"]="8a15c0",["n"]="Barranco Árido",["s"]="Barranco Árido. El Barranco Árido es un desfiladero escarpado y oculto entre los riscos rocosos del este de Durotar. Accesible únicamente a través del oscuro pasaje de una cueva desde el Cañón del Ventajo o mediante una peligrosa caída desde las alturas, esta zanja pedregosa está infestada de arpías Dustwind que anidan allí y amenazan las caravanas de suministros cercanas. Tallado en las profundidades de los riscos al este de Orgrimmar, el Barranco Árido está casi por completo aislado del tránsito habitual. Su único acceso a nivel del suelo es un estrecho túnel natural conectado con el Cañón del Ventajo. Alimentada por un modesto río, esta depresión resguardada albergó en su día un asentamiento orco pacífico, pero las bestias salvajes y los nidos de las arpías Dustwind la han convertido en un rincón sin ley en Durotar. Estas carroñeras aladas aprovechan las empinadas paredes del acantilado para anidar sus camadas y acumular mercancías robadas a las caravanas de suministros de la Horda que recorren los caminos de la región.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the ravine's roosts and recovering stolen supplies helps secure Durotar's internal trade routes against constant banditry.",["race:Orc"]="Drygulch Ravine stands as a test of frontier endurance, where young orcs prove their mettle against the ferocious harpies perched on the homeland's rocky bluffs."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Unless you survive a leap from the high cliffs above, the only ground route is through a small cave entrance tucked within neighboring Razorwind Canyon.",["al"]={"drygulch entrance","how to enter drygulch","where is the cave to drygulch"},["q"]="How do you get into Drygulch Ravine?"},{["a"]="The ravine is dominated by Dustwind harpies who build their nests, lay eggs, and stash looted caravan supplies along the craggy rock shelves.",["al"]={"drygulch mobs","what is in drygulch ravine","who lives in drygulch"},["q"]="What creatures live in Drygulch Ravine?"},{["a"]="The Dustwind harpies raid Durotar's vital trade trails, hoarding stolen cargo in the gorge. Horde authorities in Razor Hill regularly send recruits to recover provisions and cull the flock.",["al"]={"why kill harpies drygulch","drygulch ravine quests","horde interest in drygulch"},["q"]="Why does the Horde care about this ravine?"},{["a"]="Yes. A few years after the Third War, agitated thunder lizards broke out of nearby Thunder Ridge and threatened Drygulch Ravine, forcing local orcs to seek military aid from Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"thunder lizards drygulch","drygulch history lizards"},["q"]="Did thunder lizards once attack the ravine?"}},["kw"]={"drygulch ravine","durotar","dustwind harpies","harpy nests","orgrimmar","razorwind canyon","stolen supplies","thunder ridge"},["n"]="Drygulch Ravine",["s"]="Drygulch Ravine is a rugged, hidden gorge tucked into the rocky bluffs of eastern Durotar. Accessible only through an obscure cave passage from Razorwind Canyon or a perilous drop from above, this craggy trench is overrun by nesting Dustwind harpies who menace nearby supply caravans.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved deep into the crags east of Orgrimmar, Drygulch Ravine is almost entirely cut off from casual travel. Its only ground-level access is a cramped natural tunnel connected to Razorwind Canyon. Fed by a modest river, this sheltered depression once saw peaceful orc habitation, but wild beasts and roosting Dustwind harpies have turned it into a lawless pocket of Durotar. The winged scavengers use the steep cliff faces to nest their broods and stockpile stolen goods taken from Horde supply trains passing along the regional trails.",["t"]="A Bandit Haven in the Red Rocks"},{["b"]="Life in Drygulch Ravine has long been precarious. Not long after the Third War, escaped thunder lizards from Thunder Ridge threatened the area, prompting warnings to Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar. Today, the harpies pose the immediate danger. Their matriarchs fiercely defend clutches of eggs tucked along the high ledges, and Horde scouts frequently dispatch young warriors to cull the flock, recover plundered trade crates, and break the harpies' grip on the ravine.",["t"]="A Thorn in Durotar's Side"}}}}}
t["subzone:dun-algaz"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,301,27.477.0,24.503.0,40.320.0,45.296.0,44.336.0,65.229.0",["h"]="6bbd50",["n"]="Dun Algaz",["s"]="Dun Algaz. Dun Algaz es el paso de montaña fortificado y la red de túneles que conecta Loch Modan con Los Humedales. Disputada históricamente durante la Segunda Guerra, esta arteria comercial vital ha caído recientemente bajo el asedio de los orcos Faucedraco, interrumpiendo el tránsito fluido entre los territorios de Forjaz y el Puerto de Menethil. Dun Algaz es anterior a la Guerra de los Tres Martillos, ya que sirvió originalmente como el paso que el clan Martillo Salvaje utilizó para migrar hacia el norte tras ser expulsado de Forjaz. Tallado en las profundidades de los picos escarpados que separan Loch Modan de Los Humedales, el paso consta de amplios túneles de piedra, bastiones y puestos de vigilancia. Su valor estratégico es incalculable: quien controla Dun Algaz domina la única vía terrestre que une el corazón de las tierras enanas con el mar occidental en el Puerto de Menethil.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The route through Dun Algaz is critical for Alliance logistics, securing the overland road that joins the port of Menethil Harbor with Loch Modan and Ironforge.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Dun Algaz is an ancestral highway cut through the spine of Khaz Modan. Seeing Dragonmaw orcs occupy dwarven bastions and threaten supply lines to Menethil Harbor is an ongoing insult and security crisis."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dragonmaw orcs have descended from the surrounding mountains and seized control of the lower pass and stronghold. Dwarven Mountaineers have been pushed back to the upper pass near Algaz Station, leaving the main road swarming with hostile orcs who ambush travelers attempting to pass between Loch Modan and the Wetlands.",["al"]={"why are there orcs in dun algaz","dun algaz orcs","who controls dun algaz"},["q"]="Why is Dun Algaz so dangerous right now?"},{["a"]="Dun Algaz is the primary overland route connecting Ironforge and Loch Modan to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Menethil Harbor serves as the main shipping gateway between Khaz Modan and the rest of the Alliance territories, making Dun Algaz an essential corridor for supplies, troops, and trade.",["al"]={"dun algaz importance","why does ironforge need dun algaz"},["q"]="Why is this pass so important to the dwarves?"},{["a"]="Yes. Following their loss at Dun Modr, the Orcish Horde fell back across the Thandol Valley to make Dun Algaz a defensive stronghold. Sir Anduin Lothar ordered an assault to dislodge them and drive them from Khaz Modan, but the Alliance was unable to fully root out the Horde, leaving it as one of their final strongholds in the region.",["al"]={"dun algaz second war","anduin lothar dun algaz"},["q"]="Did Dun Algaz play a role in the Second War?"},{["a"]="Long before the Second War, during the ancient War of the Three Hammers, the Wildhammer dwarves were driven out of Ironforge. They traveled through Dun Algaz to migrate north into the Wetlands and eventually settle in Grim Batol.",["al"]={"wildhammer dun algaz","war of the three hammers pass"},["q"]="What is the history between Dun Algaz and the Wildhammer dwarves?"}},["kw"]={"algaz gate","algaz station","dragonmaw","dun algaz","loch modan","menethil harbor","mountain pass","wetlands"},["n"]="Dun Algaz",["s"]="Dun Algaz is the fortified mountain pass and network of tunnels connecting Loch Modan to the Wetlands. Historically contested during the Second War, this vital trade artery has recently fallen under siege by Dragonmaw orcs, cutting off easy transit between Ironforge's territories and Menethil Harbor.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Dun Algaz predates the War of the Three Hammers, originally serving as the passage the Wildhammer clan used to migrate north after being driven out of Ironforge. Carved deep into the jagged peaks separating Loch Modan and the Wetlands, the pass consists of sweeping stone tunnels, bastions, and watchposts. Its strategic value cannot be overstated: whoever holds Dun Algaz commands the only overland highway linking the dwarven heartlands to the western sea at Menethil Harbor.",["t"]="A Chokepoint Between Realms"},{["b"]="During the Second War, the Old Horde retreated to Dun Algaz after their defeat at Dun Modr, turning it into their final southern bulwark against Sir Anduin Lothar's forces. Years later, Nekros Skullcrusher sheltered the Dragonmaw clan in the surrounding caves. Though the Alliance reclaimed the pass for a time, Dragonmaw orcs have once again overrun the stronghold, forcing the dwarven Mountaineers to retreat to the upper tunnels and turning the mountain corridor into a deadly gauntlet for travelers.",["t"]="The Dragonmaw Resurgence"}}}}}
t["subzone:dun-garok"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,417,26.450.0,21.400.0,18.195.0,23.151.0,46.186.0,52.169.0",["h"]="057159",["n"]="Dun Garok",["s"]="Dun Garok. Dun Garok es un bastión montañoso y fortificado de los enanos, situado en las alturas surorientales de las Laderas de Trabalomas. Al mando del capitán Ferrocolina, la inquebrantable guarnición del puesto defiende los intereses regionales de la Alianza y operaciones cercanas como la Mina Azur frente a incursiones hostiles. Para los Renegados de Molino Tarren, esta fortaleza enana atrincherada supone una amenaza militar constante junto a sus dominios. Tallado en las escarpadas colinas del sureste de las Laderas de Trabalomas, Dun Garok se erige como un reducto fuertemente defendido por montañeros y fusileros de Forjaz. Al mando del capitán Ferrocolina, los enanos de este enclave mantienen un perímetro defensivo crucial, protegiendo los asentamientos humanos de Trabalomas y asegurando operaciones vitales en la Mina Azur. Su sólida arquitectura de piedra y sus profundos atrincheramientos proporcionan a la Alianza un punto de apoyo contra las amenazas cercanas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="This well-defended dwarven enclave poses an ongoing danger to Forsaken expansion and border security around Tarren Mill, making its garrison a priority target.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dun Garok is a proud symbol of Ironforge's reach into Lordaeron, where Captain Ironhill and his mountaineers stand resolute in defense of their human allies."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dun Garok is a fortified dwarven outpost located in the southeastern mountains of the Hillsbrad Foothills. It is manned by troops from Ironforge dedicated to defending regional Alliance holdings.",["al"]={"dun garok location","what is this dwarven keep","hillsbrad dwarf fort"},["q"]="What is Dun Garok?"},{["a"]="The stronghold is commanded by Captain Ironhill, who leads the local mountaineers and riflemen in safeguarding Hillsbrad and the nearby Azurelode Mine.",["al"]={"dun garok leader","who leads dun garok","captain ironhill"},["q"]="Who commands Dun Garok?"},{["a"]="The Forsaken view an active, fortified dwarven stronghold right on their southern border as a major security threat to Tarren Mill and actively dispatch agents to eradicate the garrison.",["al"]={"why horde attack dun garok","forsaken dun garok","tarren mill dun garok conflict"},["q"]="Why do the Forsaken want to destroy Dun Garok?"},{["a"]="Dun Garok serves as a key military anchor in Hillsbrad, helping maintain Alliance security in the region and protecting the nearby Azurelode Mine from hostile takeovers.",["al"]={"why is dun garok important","alliance purpose dun garok"},["q"]="What is Dun Garok's strategic value to the Alliance?"}},["kw"]={"azurelode mine","dun garok","dwarf","hillsbrad","ironforge","ironhill","keep","mountaineer"},["n"]="Dun Garok",["s"]="Dun Garok is a fortified dwarven mountain bastion situated in the southeastern heights of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Commanded by Captain Ironhill, the outpost's stalwart garrison defends regional Alliance interests and nearby operations like the Azurelode Mine against hostile encroachment. To the Forsaken of Tarren Mill, this entrenched dwarven stronghold stands as a constant military threat bordering their domain.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the craggy southeastern hills of Hillsbrad Foothills, Dun Garok stands as a heavily defended redoubt of Ironforge mountaineers and riflemen. Commanded by Captain Ironhill, the dwarves here maintain a critical defensive perimeter, shielding human settlements in Hillsbrad and securing vital operations at the Azurelode Mine. Their sturdy stone architecture and deep entrenchments provide the Alliance with an anchor against nearby threats.",["t"]="A Bastion in the Foothills"},{["b"]="Because of its close proximity to Tarren Mill, Dun Garok is viewed by the Forsaken as an intolerable intrusion on their southern border. Sylvanas Windrunner's forces loathe the presence of heavily armed dwarven troops so close to their stronghold, routinely plotting to infiltrate the fortress, break its defenses, and eliminate Captain Ironhill's garrison to secure Forsaken dominion over Hillsbrad.",["t"]="Target of Tarren Mill"}}}}}
t["subzone:dun-modr"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,249,19.711.0,23.604.0,29.258.0,32.197.0,48.257.0,25.208.0",["h"]="241ce5",["n"]="Dun Modr",["s"]="Dun Modr. Dun Modr es una antigua ciudad enana fortificada en el norte de los Humedales que vigila el acceso sur al Puente Thandol. Antaño una fortaleza crucial defendida y disputada a lo largo de múltiples guerras, ha caído recientemente ante una fuerza hostil de enanos Hierro Negro. Situada en el extremo norte de los Humedales, Dun Modr domina la principal vía terrestre que une Khaz Modan con los reinos humanos del norte. Debido a esta ubicación vital, la fortaleza ha presenciado un intenso derramamiento de sangre a lo largo de las décadas. Durante la Segunda Guerra, la Horda orca la capturó y se atrincheró en el bastión enano, utilizándolo como base de operaciones avanzada para lanzar incursiones y repeler a los ejércitos de la Alianza. Los guerreros de Stromgarde lanzaron un brutal asalto anfibio desde Tol Barad para recuperarla, pero los orcos contraatacaron en un sangriento toma y daca. Las fuerzas de la Alianza lideradas por Lord Anduin Lothar finalmente expulsaron a los invasores hacia el sur a través del Puente Thandol, devolviendo la custodia del bastión a los enanos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The fall of Dun Modr threatens the critical transit route across the Thandol Span, severing easy travel between Ironforge and the northern Alliance remnants.",["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a storied Bronzebeard mountain settlement fall into the hands of the treacherous Dark Iron clan is a bitter insult that demands vengeance."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dun Modr sits directly along the major northern road in the Wetlands leading to the Thandol Span. Controlling the fortress means controlling all overland traffic, supply lines, and military movement between Khaz Modan and the northern continent of Lordaeron.",["al"]={"why does dun modr matter","importance of dun modr","dun modr strategic value"},["q"]="Why is Dun Modr so important?"},{["a"]="The stronghold has fallen to the Dark Iron clan, led on-site by a warlock named Balgaras the Foul. Bronzebeard Mountaineers loyal to Ironforge maintain a watchful camp nearby, hoping to reclaim it.",["al"]={"who is in dun modr","who runs dun modr","who lives in dun modr"},["q"]="Who controls Dun Modr right now?"},{["a"]="The Orcish Horde overran the town and turned it into a forward military base. Stromgarde forces struck from the island of Tol Barad to retake the ruins, sparking fierce clashes until Anduin Lothar's Alliance forces finally swept the Horde out of the region.",["al"]={"second war dun modr","orcs in dun modr","did horde take dun modr"},["q"]="What happened to Dun Modr during the Second War?"},{["a"]="Balgaras the Foul is the Dark Iron warlock leading the occupation of Dun Modr. Under his command, the Dark Irons managed to damage the Thandol Span and drive the local Ironforge defenders out of the fortress.",["al"]={"balgaras the foul lore","balgaras who","dark iron leader dun modr"},["q"]="Who is Balgaras the Foul?"}},["kw"]={"balgaras the foul","dark iron","dun modr","ironforge","mountaineers","thandol span","wetlands"},["n"]="Dun Modr",["s"]="Dun Modr is an ancient fortified dwarven town in northern Wetlands, guarding the southern approach to the Thandol Span. Once a critical fortress held and contested across multiple wars, it has recently fallen to a hostile force of Dark Iron dwarves.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated at the northern edge of the Wetlands, Dun Modr commands the primary overland highway linking Khaz Modan with the northern human kingdoms. Because of this vital location, the stronghold has seen heavy bloodshed over the decades. During the Second War, the Orcish Horde captured and entrenched themselves within the dwarven fortress, using it as a forward staging ground to launch raids and repel Alliance armies. Stromgarde warriors launched a brutal amphibious assault from Tol Barad to reclaim it, only for the Orcs to strike back in a bloody tug-of-war. Alliance forces led by Lord Anduin Lothar ultimately drove the invaders south across the Thandol Span, restoring dwarven custody over the bastion.",["t"]="A Contested Bastion"},{["b"]="With Ironforge's attention divided and many of its finest mountaineers committed to Alliance duties abroad, Dun Modr was left vulnerable. Seizing the opportunity, Dark Iron invaders pushed north and sabotaged the Thandol Span with explosives before swarming the fortress. Under the command of the Dark Iron warlock Balgaras the Foul, these infiltrators overran the town's defenders, driving out the Bronzebeard garrison and transforming the strategic outpost into a hostile den. Surrounding Mountaineers now maintain a grim perimeter just down the road, desperately seeking aid to dislodge the occupiers.",["t"]="The Dark Iron Incursion"}}}}}
t["subzone:durnholde-keep"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,286,23.665.0,32.442.0,31.269.0,38.203.0,43.258.0,54.214.0",["h"]="c6870f",["n"]="Castillo de Durnholde",["s"]="Castillo de Durnholde. El Castillo de Durnholde es una fortaleza devastada situada al este de Molino Tarren, en las Laderas de Trabalomas. Antaño centro neurálgico de los campos de internamiento de orcos de la Alianza y lugar donde el Jefe de Guerra Thrall fue criado como gladiador cautivo, hoy yace en ruinas, ocupado por los forajidos de la Hermandad. Construido por la Alianza, Durnholde sirvió como cuartel general para supervisar los campos de internamiento del sur tras la Segunda Guerra. Bajo el mando del ambicioso y corrupto teniente general Aedelas Blackmoore, funcionaba tanto de fortaleza administrativa como de arena de gladiadores. Fue aquí donde Blackmoore crio al infante huérfano Go'el, dándole el nombre de Thrall y adiestrándolo para combatir por diversión y beneficio económico. Con la ayuda de Taretha Foxton, Thrall escapó de su cautiverio y más tarde unió a los dispersos clanes orcos bajo el estandarte de la nueva Horda. Al regresar a Durnholde, Thrall sitió la fortaleza, abatió a Blackmoore y suplicó a los espíritus de la tierra que derribaran sus muros.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Once a linchpin of Lordaeron's defense and justice, Durnholde's shattered ramparts now serve only as a wretched lair for Syndicate outlaws and cutthroats.",["race:Orc"]="The ruined stones of Durnholde mark the forge where Warchief Thrall threw off his chains, ending decades of orcish captivity and kindling the rebirth of the Horde."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Thrall returned to Durnholde at the head of the liberated Horde to defeat his former master, Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore. After slaying Blackmoore, Thrall communed with the spirits of the earth to demolish the fortress so it could never again cage his people.",["al"]={"who destroyed durnholde","what happened to durnholde keep","why is durnholde destroyed"},["q"]="Why is Durnholde Keep in ruins?"},{["a"]="The stronghold is held by the Syndicate, a faction of exiled Alterac nobles turned outlaws. They use the crumbling ramparts as a fortified redoubt to conduct banditry and launch attacks across Hillsbrad.",["al"]={"who lives in durnholde","durnholde mobs","syndicate at durnholde"},["q"]="Who currently occupies Durnholde Keep?"},{["a"]="Aedelas Blackmoore discovered the orphaned orc as a child and raised him at Durnholde as a slave. Thrall was educated in tactics and forced to fight as a gladiator in the arena before he managed to break out with help from a human woman named Taretha Foxton.",["al"]={"did thrall live here","thrall durnholde history","was thrall a prisoner here"},["q"]="What was Thrall's connection to this place?"},{["a"]="Beyond serving as an Alliance stronghold, it was used as a prison facility. During the conflict, the forest troll warlord Zul'jin was held captive here until Orgrim Doomhammer breached the fortress to liberate him.",["al"]={"durnholde second war","what was durnholde used for"},["q"]="What purpose did the keep serve during the Second War?"}},["kw"]={"blackmoore","durnholde keep","hillsbrad","internment","syndicate","taretha foxton","tarren mill","thrall"},["n"]="Durnholde Keep",["s"]="Durnholde Keep is a shattered fortress situated east of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once the nerve center of the Alliance's orc internment camps and the place where Warchief Thrall was raised as a captive gladiator, it now lies in ruin, occupied by outlaws of the Syndicate.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Built by the Alliance, Durnholde served as the headquarters overseeing the southern internment camps following the Second War. Commanded by the ambitious and corrupt Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore, it functioned as both an administrative fortress and a gladiatorial arena. It was here that Blackmoore raised the orphaned infant Go'el, naming him Thrall and training him to fight for sport and profit. Aided by Taretha Foxton, Thrall escaped captivity and later united the dispersed orc clans under the banner of the new Horde. Returning to Durnholde, Thrall laid siege to the fortress, slew Blackmoore, and called upon the earth spirits to shatter its walls.",["t"]="A Crucible of Captivity"},{["b"]="Since its collapse prior to the Third War, Durnholde Keep has remained a scarred heap of masonry. In the vacuum left by Lordaeron's fall, the aristocratic bandits of the Syndicate took refuge among the ramparts. Operating out of the broken bailey and towers, these dispossessed Alterac nobles and cutthroats prey upon travelers across the Hillsbrad Foothills, turning a former instrument of martial law into a heavily fortified rogue outpost.",["t"]="In the Clutches of the Syndicate"}}}}}
t["subzone:dust-plains"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,225,17.466.0,34.166.0,51.152.0,52.100.0,64.204.0",["h"]="6b8478",["n"]="Los Yermos Polvorientos",["s"]="Los Yermos Polvorientos. Los Yermos Polvorientos forman la frontera meridional de Páramos de Poniente, seca y azotada por el viento. Marcada por un terreno árido y matorrales escasos, la región está invadida por agresivos campamentos de gnolls y limita con la vieja torre de un mago a lo largo de su elevación oriental. Extendiéndose por el sur de Páramos de Poniente, Los Yermos Polvorientos marcan la transición entre las convulsas tierras de cultivo y un páramo desolado. A diferencia de las granjas saqueadas del norte, esta árida extensión lleva mucho tiempo abandonada a manadas de gnolls salvajes que tienden emboscadas a los viajeros y desafían a cualquiera que se aventure hacia la costa o las colinas cercanas. En el límite oriental se alza Torre de Klaven, un solitario refugio mágico que no ofrece cobijo frente a las bestias que merodean por los yermos circundantes.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Dust Plains represent another lawless fringe where Stormwind's neglect is starkly visible, forcing travelers and local defenders to fend off relentless gnoll packs without official reinforcement."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Dust Plains occupy the southernmost portion of Westfall, lying south of the abandoned farmsteads and extending toward the cliffs and Mortwake's Tower on the east.",["al"]={"dust plains location","where is dust plains","where dust plains"},["q"]="Where are the Dust Plains located?"},{["a"]="The region is heavily populated by savage gnolls, who maintain crude camps throughout the dusty landscape and violently assault anyone who wanders near.",["al"]={"what lives in dust plains","dust plains enemies","mobs in dust plains"},["q"]="What threats can travelers find in the Dust Plains?"},{["a"]="That is Mortwake's Tower, an old wizard's spire that overlooks the eastern verge of the Dust Plains.",["al"]={"dust plains tower","eastern tower westfall","what is mortwake's tower"},["q"]="What is the tower on the eastern edge of the plains?"},{["a"]="No. The People's Militia is already stretched dangerously thin defending Sentinel Hill and the northern farms from the Defias Brotherhood, leaving the Dust Plains entirely in the hands of prowling gnolls.",["al"]={"militia dust plains","is westfall guard here"},["q"]="Does the People's Militia hold any control over the Dust Plains?"}},["kw"]={"dust plains","gnolls","mortwake's tower","plains","southern westfall","westfall"},["n"]="Dust Plains",["s"]="The Dust Plains form the dry, wind-scoured southern frontier of Westfall. Marked by arid ground and scarce scrub, the region is overrun by aggressive gnoll encampments and borders an old wizard's tower along its eastern rise.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching across southern Westfall, the Dust Plains mark the transition from troubled farmland to desolate wilderness. Unlike the plundered farmsteads to the north, this arid reach has long been surrendered to packs of feral gnolls who ambush travelers and challenge anyone venturing toward the coast or the nearby hills. On the eastern boundary sits Mortwake's Tower, a lonely magical retreat that offers no shelter from the beasts prowling the surrounding wastes.",["t"]="A Barren Frontier"}}}}}
t["subzone:dustwind-cave"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,245,22.435.0,18.354.0,31.116.0,27.158.0,40.198.0,42.166.0",["h"]="32ef8d",["n"]="Cueva Viento Seco",["s"]="Cueva Viento Seco. La Cueva Viento Seco es una hondonada apartada situada en lo alto de los acantilados del Cañón del Ventajo, justo al noreste de Cerrotajo. Sirve como campo de entrenamiento activo y santuario secreto para los iniciados de la nefasta secta Filo Ardiente que opera en Durotar. Con vistas al Cañón del Ventajo, la Cueva Viento Seco es una de las amenazas más cercanas y peligrosas para Cerrotajo. Aunque muchos asumen que los sectarios demoníacos solo se reúnen en las profundidades subterráneas, aquí el Filo Ardiente entrena a nuevos reclutas ante las mismísimas narices de las autoridades de la Horda. Sectarios sombríos instruyen a los iniciados en magias oscuras prohibidas y demonología, preparándolos para socavar el joven reino orco desde el interior de las fronteras de Durotar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks of the Horde will recognize the dark rituals taking place within Dustwind Cave, though the Burning Blade wields their fel gifts toward rebellion rather than the service of Thrall's new order.",["faction:Horde"]="Dustwind Cave represents an embarrassing and dangerous internal breach, harboring demon cultists within shouting distance of Razor Hill."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dustwind Cave is situated high along the clifftops of Razorwind Canyon, directly northeast of Razor Hill in Durotar.",["al"]={"dustwind cave location","where is dustwind cave","how to find dustwind cave"},["q"]="Where is Dustwind Cave located?"},{["a"]="The cave is occupied by cultists and initiates of the Burning Blade, a shadowy demonic cult dedicated to spreading fel corruption and destabilizing the Horde.",["al"]={"who is in dustwind cave","dustwind cave enemies","mobs in dustwind cave"},["q"]="Who occupies Dustwind Cave?"},{["a"]="The Burning Blade uses Dustwind Cave as a secluded training outpost where seasoned cultists instruct new recruits in demonic arts away from the immediate gaze of the Orgrimmar and Razor Hill guards.",["al"]={"why are cultists in dustwind cave","burning blade purpose durotar"},["q"]="Why is the Burning Blade operating here?"},{["a"]="Having demon-worshiping cultists lurking just steps away from Razor Hill poses an unacceptable security risk to traveling recruits and the overall defense of Durotar.",["al"]={"why clear dustwind cave","horde threat dustwind cave"},["q"]="Why does the Horde want this cave cleared?"}},["kw"]={"burning blade","cultists","durotar","dustwind cave","felblood","razor hill","razorwind canyon"},["n"]="Dustwind Cave",["s"]="Dustwind Cave is a secluded hollow perched atop the cliffs of Razorwind Canyon, just northeast of Razor Hill. It serves as an active training ground and covert sanctuary for initiates of the nefarious Burning Blade cult operating within Durotar.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Overlooking Razorwind Canyon, Dustwind Cave is one of the closest and most perilous threats to Razor Hill. While many assume demonic cultists gather only in deep subterranean depths, here the Burning Blade trains fresh recruits right under the noses of the Horde authorities. Shadowy cultists tutor initiates in forbidden dark magics and demonology, preparing them to undermine the young orcish realm from within Durotar's own borders.",["t"]="A Shadow in the Cliffs"},{["b"]="Those who trespass into the cave risk exposure to the cultists' dangerous corruptions. Practitioners inside channel volatile dark arts such as felblood afflictions, demonstrating how deeply the Burning Blade clings to the demonic legacy Thrall fought so hard to banish. Eliminating the cabal here is vital for maintaining the precarious peace of Durotar.",["t"]="Tainted Bloodlines"}}}}}
t["subzone:dwarven-district"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,318,27.709.0,44.284.0,38.177.0,53.200.0,37.159.0",["h"]="162d0d",["n"]="Distrito de los Enanos",["s"]="Distrito de los Enanos. Enclavado en el rincón norte de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, el Distrito de los Enanos es un bullicioso enclave industrial repleto de hornos rugientes, yunques resonantes y un denso humo. Establecido por artesanos de Forjaz que acudieron para ayudar a reconstruir la capital tras la Segunda Guerra, actúa como el palpitante corazón mecánico de la ciudad. Tras la devastación de la Segunda Guerra, el Rey Magni Barbabronce envió a cientos de artesanos, canteros e ingenieros enanos al sur para ayudar a sus aliados humanos a reconstruir Ventormenta. En lugar de dispersarse por toda la capital, establecieron su propio enclave en el barrio norte. Hoy en día, el distrito conserva el inconfundible carácter de Forjaz, dominado por una sólida cantería, extensas fundiciones y bulliciosos talleres de artesanía. Entre el calor de Armaduras de Placas de Potts y las charlas de taberna en El Barril Dorado, el enclave ofrece un refugio familiar para los viajeros de Khaz Modan. También alberga el portal de Ventormenta hacia el Tren subterráneo, enlazando la capital humana directamente con Forjaz.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The district provides Stormwind's most capable smithing facilities, equipped with expansive smelting forges, sturdy anvils, and veteran instructors.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves far from Khaz Modan, this district offers a familiar comfort: the roar of working blast furnaces, stout ale at The Golden Keg, and quick passage back to Ironforge."},["faq"]={{["a"]="After Stormwind was destroyed during the First War and retaken in the Second War, King Magni Bronzebeard sent dwarven craftsmen and laborers south to aid in the capital's reconstruction. The workers settled in this northern sector, building workshops and homes suited to their tastes.",["al"]={"why dwarves in stormwind","dwarf area origin","why is it called dwarven district"},["q"]="Why is there a dwarven enclave in Stormwind?"},{["a"]="On the eastern side of the district, an open arched tunnel leads directly into the Deeprun Tram station. This subterranean marvel connects Stormwind to Ironforge within minutes.",["al"]={"how to get to ironforge","where is the tram","deeprun tram entrance"},["q"]="How do you get to Ironforge from here?"},{["a"]="Given its industrial character, the district is the city's premier hub for mining, blacksmithing, and engineering. It features heavy forges, anvils, and dedicated trainers for these craft disciplines.",["al"]={"professions dwarven district","trainers in dwarven district","blacksmith trainer stormwind"},["q"]="What professions are trained in the Dwarven District?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's hunters make their headquarters in the Dwarven District's Hunter's Guild, fittingly sharing quarters and trade supplies alongside dwarven marksmen.",["al"]={"hunter trainer stormwind","hunter lodge","stormwind hunter guild"},["q"]="Where can hunters train in Stormwind?"}},["kw"]={"deeprun tram","dwarven district","hunters guild","ironforge","magni bronzebeard","potts plates","stormwind","the golden keg"},["n"]="Dwarven District",["s"]="Tucked into the northern corner of Stormwind City, the Dwarven District is a bustling industrial enclave filled with roaring furnaces, ringing anvils, and thick smog. Established by Ironforge craftsmen who arrived to help rebuild the capital after the Second War, it serves as the beating mechanical heart of the city.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Following the devastation of the Second War, King Magni Bronzebeard sent hundreds of dwarven artisans, stonemasons, and engineers south to assist their human allies in rebuilding Stormwind. Rather than dispersing throughout the capital, they established their own enclave in the northern quarter. Today, the district retains the unmistakable character of Ironforge, dominated by heavy stone masonry, sprawling smelting operations, and bustling craft shops. Between the heat of Potts' Plates and the tavern chatter of The Golden Keg, the enclave provides a familiar haven for travelers from Khaz Modan. It also houses the Stormwind portal to the Deeprun Tram, tethering the human capital directly to Ironforge.",["t"]="A Home Away from Khaz Modan"}}}}}
t["subzone:eastvale-logging-camp"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="21,317,29.561.0,28.585.0,50.232.0,50.259.0,23.203.0,44.137.0",["h"]="d28738",["n"]="Aserradero de la Vega del Este",["s"]="Aserradero de la Vega del Este. El Aserradero de la Vega del Este es un asentamiento maderero vital enclavado en los bosques orientales del Bosque de Elwynn, cerca de la frontera con las Montañas Crestagrana. El campamento suministra madera esencial a Ventormenta y a los asentamientos circundantes, pero sus operaciones se ven constantemente obstaculizadas por depredadores hambrientos que merodean por los bosques cercanos. Los pedidos de madera llegan constantemente al Aserradero de la Vega del Este de parte de compradores de todo el Reino de Ventormenta, pero cumplir estos plazos tan estrictos es una tarea angustiosa. La densa espesura que rodea el campamento rebosa de lobos feroces y osos al acecho que a menudo ahuyentan a los leñadores de sus puestos de trabajo, dejando valiosa madera cortada abandonada en el bosque. Bajo la dirección del Supervisor Raelen, el campamento recurre con frecuencia a aventureros errantes para diezmar a las bestias invasoras y recuperar la madera caída antes de que las entregas sufran retrasos irreparables.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Eastvale Logging Camp is one of the premier locations in Elwynn Forest where Alliance members can purchase dependable Stormwind steeds.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, Eastvale provides the essential timber that continues to rebuild and maintain the kingdom's settlements."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Eastvale serves as the primary timber source in eastern Elwynn Forest for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Lumberjacks here work long hours under strict deadlines to fulfill heavy demands for wood from builders and nobles across the realm.",["al"]={"why is eastvale here","what is eastvale","eastvale lumber role"},["q"]="What is the main purpose of Eastvale Logging Camp?"},{["a"]="Dense woods surround the camp, and aggressive wild bears and prowling wolves constantly menace the workers. The attacks often force the woodcutters to flee, leaving chopped timber behind and putting timber orders at serious risk of missing shipment deadlines.",["al"]={"eastvale problems","why do loggers need help","wolves at eastvale"},["q"]="Why is the logging camp always hiring adventurers?"},{["a"]="Marshal Haggard is the retired former leader of the Stormwind Guard. He stepped down from service a few years ago and now resides in a peaceful estate on the bluffs overlooking the Eastvale Logging Camp.",["al"]={"haggard","old man near eastvale","marshal haggard elwynn"},["q"]="Who is Marshal Haggard?"},{["a"]="Yes. The logging camp features an active horse-breeding stable where Alliance adventurers can purchase riding horses and riding training.",["al"]={"horse vendor eastvale","eastvale horses","buy mount elwynn"},["q"]="Can you buy mounts at Eastvale Logging Camp?"}},["kw"]={"eastvale","elwynn","haggard","horses","logging camp","lumber","raelen","timber","tremaind"},["n"]="Eastvale Logging Camp",["s"]="Eastvale Logging Camp is a vital lumber settlement tucked into the eastern woodlands of Elwynn Forest, near the border with the Redridge Mountains. The camp supplies vital timber to Stormwind and surrounding settlements, but its operations are constantly hampered by hungry predators prowling the surrounding forests.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Orders for timber constantly stream into Eastvale Logging Camp from buyers across the Kingdom of Stormwind, but meeting these strict deadlines is a harrowing task. The dense wilderness surrounding the camp swarms with vicious wolves and prowling bears that routinely chase lumberjacks away from their worksites, leaving valuable cut timber abandoned in the woods. Under the direction of Supervisor Raelen, the camp frequently relies on wandering adventurers to cull the encroaching beasts and retrieve fallen wood before deliveries fall fatally behind schedule.",["t"]="A Vital Operation Under Siege"},{["b"]="Despite its remote location, Eastvale is more than just a logging outpost. It features several residential dwellings and bustling horse stables where travelers can purchase fine mounts. The lumber trade here is closely tied to Stormwind nobility, including Lord Joran Tremaind, whose family maintains significant business interests in the camp's timber harvest. On a nearby hill overlooking the worksite sits the quiet manor of retired Marshal Haggard, the former leader of the Stormwind Guard, who withdrew to this rustic outpost to live out his retirement away from capital politics.",["t"]="Life on the Eastern Frontier"}}}}}
t["subzone:echo-isles"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,320,21.590.0,15.488.0,51.308.0,16.224.0,32.185.0,63.214.0",["h"]="cc9690",["n"]="Islas del Eco",["s"]="Islas del Eco. Las Islas del Eco son un conjunto de islas tropicales situadas justo frente a la costa suroriental de Durotar. Colonizado originalmente por los trols de Lanza Negra tras huir de sus islas ancestrales, el archipiélago se encuentra actualmente bajo el control del médico brujo renegado Zalazane, quien expulsó a su pueblo al exilio valiéndose de magia oscura y esbirros esclavizados. Tras su huida a través del Mare Magnum junto a Thrall, la tribu Lanza Negra reclamó las Islas del Eco como su nuevo hogar. Su paz se vio truncada en repetidas ocasiones: primero por las fuerzas navales del Gran Almirante Daelin Valiente durante la invasión de Durotar por parte de Kul Tiras, y más tarde desde dentro. Poco después de que los trols repelieran la flota de Valiente, uno de sus propios médicos brujos, Zalazane, recurrió a las artes oscuras para esclavizar las mentes de sus congéneres. El caudillo Vol'jin y los Lanza Negra libres se vieron obligados a abandonar las islas una vez más, buscando refugio temporal al otro lado del estrecho en el Poblado Sen'jin.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Securing the Echo Isles is essential for stabilizing the southern coast of Durotar, protecting Sen'jin Village, and consolidating the young Horde's borders against naval threats and rogue mystics.",["race:Troll"]="The Echo Isles represent both the promised home of the Darkspear in Kalimdor and the bitter sting of Zalazane's betrayal. Reclaiming them is a matter of tribal survival and personal honor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The witch doctor Zalazane betrayed the tribe, using dark magic to strip his brethren of their free will and twist them into obedient servitors. Chieftain Vol'jin ordered an evacuation to the mainland coast of Durotar, founding Sen'jin Village as a staging ground while the tribe fights to reclaim their home.",["al"]={"why abandoned","why did trolls leave","troll home"},["q"]="Why don't the Darkspear trolls live here right now?"},{["a"]="Zalazane is a traitorous Darkspear witch doctor who turned on his tribe. Using powerful voodoo and dark magic, he placed hexes over the islands, corrupted the local wildlife, and enslaved fellow trolls into mindless thralls.",["al"]={"who is zalazane","boss on echo isles","witch doctor zalazane"},["q"]="Who is Zalazane?"},{["a"]="The archipelago is infested with wild raptors, tigers, and corrupted beasts, as well as Zalazane's voodoo heaps and his mind-controlled troll minions, including hexed and voodoo trolls.",["al"]={"echo isles mobs","what is on the islands","echo isles dangers"},["q"]="What threats are on the islands?"},{["a"]="After Thrall and the Horde rescued the Darkspear tribe from a sinking island and hostile naga in the Great Sea, the trolls journeyed to Kalimdor and were granted the Echo Isles to settle alongside their orc allies.",["al"]={"how did trolls get here","darkspear origin","echo isles history"},["q"]="How did the Darkspear tribe end up on these islands originally?"}},["kw"]={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","trolls","vol'jin","voodoo","zalazane"},["n"]="Echo Isles",["s"]="The Echo Isles are a cluster of tropical islands lying just off the southeastern coast of Durotar. Originally settled by the Darkspear trolls after fleeing their ancestral islands, the archipelago is currently lost to the rogue witch doctor Zalazane, who drove his people into exile with dark magic and enslaved minions.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Following their flight across the Great Sea alongside Thrall, the Darkspear tribe claimed the Echo Isles as their new home. Their peace was repeatedly shattered: first by the naval forces of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore during Kul Tiras' invasion of Durotar, and later from within. Shortly after the trolls drove back Proudmoore's fleet, one of their own witch doctors, Zalazane, seized dark arts to enslave the minds of his kin. Chieftain Vol'jin and the free Darkspears were forced to abandon the islands once more, seeking temporary refuge across the narrow strait at Sen'jin Village.",["t"]="A Fractured Sanctuary"},{["b"]="Today, the tropical cluster is overrun by aggressive predators, tainted wildlife, and the thralls of Zalazane. Using malevolent hexes, voodoo fetishes, and ju-ju heaps placed throughout the islands, the traitorous witch doctor bends beasts and captive trolls to his will. From their encampment at Darkspear Strand, Vol'jin's scouts and warriors mount frequent sorties into the islands, determined to recover the remains of their fallen and strike down the mad mystic who stole their home.",["t"]="Zalazane's Grip"}}}}}
t["subzone:echo-ridge-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,235,21.427.0,29.298.0,35.177.0,41.203.0,33.146.0",["h"]="753b20",["n"]="Mina del Eco",["s"]="Mina del Eco. La Mina del Eco es una pequeña excavación horadada en los acantilados noroccidentales del Valle de Villanorte. Rica en piedra y mineral, recientemente ha caído en las garras de una destructiva plaga de kóbold, lo que ha paralizado las operaciones locales de Villanorte. Oculta en las colinas sobre la Abadía de Villanorte, la Mina del Eco debía abastecer al valle con piedra y metal útiles. En su lugar, oportunistas kóbold pulularon por los túneles y expulsaron a los trabajadores locales. El Alguacil McBride considera la infestación como un riesgo de seguridad inaceptable para la tranquilidad de Villanorte y los esfuerzos de reclutamiento, enviando a los nuevos reclutas directamente a los túneles para reducir sus números y recuperar el lugar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Mining"]="The shafts of Echo Ridge are rich in early mineral deposits, though any prospector seeking ore will have to fight through hordes of candle-bearing kobolds first.",["race:Human"]="For fresh recruits answering Stormwind's call, purging Echo Ridge Mine serves as an essential trial by fire to defend Northshire Abbey."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kobolds are natural burrowers drawn to dark, mineral-rich tunnels. Sensing weak defenses, they overran Echo Ridge Mine to dig for treasures and claim the territory as their own.",["al"]={"why kobolds here","echo ridge kobolds","who took the mine"},["q"]="Why are kobolds in Echo Ridge Mine?"},{["a"]="Marshal McBride at Northshire Abbey oversees efforts to clear the mine. He enlists newly arrived adventurers to scout the tunnels and cull the infesting vermin before they expand further into the valley.",["al"]={"who wants echo ridge back","echo ridge quests","mcbride echo ridge"},["q"]="Who is trying to reclaim Echo Ridge Mine?"},{["a"]="The mine entrance sits in the northwestern corner of Northshire Valley, carved directly into the rocky hillside just north of the abbey vineyards.",["al"]={"echo ridge location","where is echo ridge","find echo ridge mine"},["q"]="Where is Echo Ridge Mine located?"}},["kw"]={"echo ridge","echo ridge mine","kobold","marshal mcbride","mine","northshire","northshire valley"},["n"]="Echo Ridge Mine",["s"]="Echo Ridge Mine is a small excavation carved into the northwestern cliffs of Northshire Valley. Rich in stone and ore, it has recently fallen into the clutches of a destructive kobold infestation, halting Northshire's local operations.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the hills above Northshire Abbey, Echo Ridge Mine was meant to supply the valley with useful stone and metal. Instead, opportunistic kobolds swarmed through the tunnels, driving out the local workers. Marshal McBride views the infestation as an unacceptable security risk to Northshire's safety and recruitment efforts, directing new recruits straight into the tunnels to cull their numbers and reclaim the site.",["t"]="A Foothold for Vermin"},{["b"]="The occupation of Echo Ridge is part of a broader pattern of kobold encroachment spreading across Elwynn Forest. If left unchecked in the northwestern ridge, these subterranean pests threaten to disrupt Northshire's peaceful training grounds and choke off crucial resources from reaching the abbey.",["t"]="The Threat Beneath Northshire"}}}}}
t["subzone:elder-rise"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,292,30.550.0,21.480.0,28.204.0,35.201.0,37.258.0,28.163.0",["h"]="8c2a5d",["n"]="Alto de los Ancestros",["s"]="Alto de los Ancestros. El Alto de los Ancestros se encuentra directamente al este de la meseta central de Cima del Trueno, accesible a través de largos puentes colgantes tanto desde High Rise como desde Middle Rise. Sirve como el corazón espiritual de la capital tauren, albergando al Círculo Cenarion, a druidas y sacerdotes tauren, y al Consejo de Ancianos gobernante. Conectado a las mesetas principales por oscilantes puentes de cuerda, el Alto de los Ancestros está dedicado a la reflexión tranquila, la sabiduría sagrada y el gobierno cívico. Los druidas y sacerdotes tauren se reúnen aquí para enseñar a los acólitos los caminos de la naturaleza y la devoción espiritual. En lo alto de esta meseta reside el Archidruida Hamuul Runatótem, el venerado líder que devolvió el druidismo al pueblo tauren y forjó estrechos lazos con el Círculo Cenarion. Junto a estos santuarios salvajes se alza la Sala de los Ancianos, donde los líderes tribales se reúnen para deliberar sobre los asuntos que afronta su incipiente capital.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Elder Rise is the paramount home for Horde druids, serving as Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem's sanctuary and the Cenarion Circle's regional seat in Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="The rise houses the Council of Elders and spiritual guides who steer your tribes through peace, tradition, and the complex realities of the Horde."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Elder Rise serves as the center for spiritual learning and civic deliberation in Thunder Bluff. It houses the Cenarion Circle's druids, tauren priests, the governing Council of Elders, and tribal leaders.",["al"]={"purpose of elder rise","what is on elder rise","elder rise buildings"},["q"]="What is Elder Rise used for?"},{["a"]="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem resides here. A close friend and advisor to Cairne Bloodhoof, Hamuul is the highest-ranking tauren in the Cenarion Circle and trains those called to walk the path of nature.",["al"]={"archdruid thunder bluff","tauren druid leader","hamuul location"},["q"]="Who leads the druids on Elder Rise?"},{["a"]="Magatha Grimtotem occupies a tent situated between the bridges. As the elder crone and chieftain of the Grimtotem tribe, she attends the Council of Elders to represent her people in Thunder Bluff, despite mutual distrust between her clan and Cairne's allies.",["al"]={"where is magatha","magatha grimtotem location","grimtotem on elder rise"},["q"]="Why does Magatha Grimtotem stay here?"},{["a"]="Elder Rise lies directly east of the city's central plateau. It can be reached via large wooden rope bridges connected to both the High Rise and the lower plateau.",["al"]={"getting to elder rise","elder rise bridges","directions elder rise"},["q"]="How do you reach Elder Rise?"}},["kw"]={"cenarion circle","elder rise","hall of elders","hamuul runetotem","magatha grimtotem","mulgore","thunder bluff"},["n"]="Elder Rise",["s"]="Elder Rise sits directly east of Thunder Bluff's central plateau, reachable across long suspension bridges from both the High and Middle Rises. It serves as the spiritual heart of the tauren capital, hosting the Cenarion Circle, tauren druids and priests, and the governing Council of Elders.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Connected to the main mesas by swaying rope bridges, Elder Rise is dedicated to quiet reflection, sacred wisdom, and civic governance. Tauren druids and priests gather here to teach acolytes the ways of nature and spiritual devotion. High atop this mesa resides Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem, the revered leader who brought druidism back to the tauren people and forged close ties with the Cenarion Circle. Alongside these wild sanctuaries stands the Hall of Elders, where tribal leaders convene to deliberate on matters facing their fledgling capital.",["t"]="Sanctuary of Faith and Council"},{["b"]="Despite its role as a peaceful sanctuary, political tension lingers over the rise. Magatha Grimtotem, elder matriarch of the secretive and haughty Grimtotem tribe, maintains her residence in a hut positioned between the two bridges. While Cairne Bloodhoof extends hospitality and formal council seats to all tauren lineages, her watchful presence serves as a constant reminder that not every tribe embraces the Bloodhoof's pacifist ideals or unquestioning alliance with the Horde.",["t"]="A Precarious Presence"}}}}}
t["subzone:engineering-labs"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,323,29.404.0,16.387.0,51.240.0,43.246.0,48.255.0,53.198.0",["h"]="5d27f6",["n"]="Laboratorios de Ingeniería",["s"]="Laboratorios de Ingeniería. Los Laboratorios de Ingeniería son una instalación de investigación y manufactura de varios niveles situada en las profundidades de Gnomeregan. Conectado con la Entrada del Taller y el Hangar de Lanzamiento, este bullicioso centro de innovación gnómica fue arrasado durante el cataclismo radiactivo de la ciudad y ahora está plagado de enloquecidos gnomos parias y artefactos mecánicos descontrolados. Construidos alrededor de una estructura mecánica central, los Laboratorios de Ingeniería abarcan dos niveles principales conectados por un elevador de carga central. En el apogeo de Gnomeregan, los manitas desarrollaban aquí esquemas y perfeccionaban inventos de relojería. En la actualidad, las fugas de radiación han vuelto locos a los investigadores supervivientes, transformándolos en desquiciados gnomos parias que custodian mecánicamente maquinaria averiada junto a ensamblajes descontrolados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="The Engineering Labs represent the pinnacle of fallen gnomish automation, retaining functional automated punchograph terminals and discarded schematics amid the wreckage.",["race:Gnome"]="For exiled gnomes, these laboratories are a tragic sight: once the beating heart of their race's technological triumphs, now reduced to an irradiated ruin overrun by their corrupted kin."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Before the city fell, the Engineering Labs were dedicated to research, assembly, and testing of complex gnome contraptions and automated devices. Gnomish engineers and technicians used the vast two-level chamber to blueprint new technology.",["al"]={"purpose of engineering labs","what was made here","engineering labs lore"},["q"]="What were the Engineering Labs originally used for?"},{["a"]="Irradiated leper gnomes and haywire mechanical automatons roam both tiers of the chamber. These lingering residents were driven completely mad by the irradiated gas released during the city's fall and attack any non-irradiated intruders on sight.",["al"]={"who is inside","enemies in engineering labs","monsters here"},["q"]="What threats roam the Engineering Labs now?"},{["a"]="These automated gnomish data terminals are found on the lower level of the Engineering Labs. They allow engineers and adventurers to punch encoded data cards, advancing their security clearance and deciphering technical archives preserved within the city.",["al"]={"punchograph d","matrix punchograph 3005-d","yellow card machine"},["q"]="What are the Matrix Punchograph 3005-D machines?"},{["a"]="The upper level connects directly to the Workshop Entrance back door and passages leading to the Launch Bay. The lower level leads to the main corridors connecting the Launch Bay and Tinkers' Court.",["al"]={"where does this lead","engineering labs exits","routes to engineering labs"},["q"]="How does this area connect to the rest of Gnomeregan?"}},["kw"]={"engineering labs","gnomeregan","launch bay","leper gnome","punchograph","tinkers court","workshop entrance"},["n"]="Engineering Labs",["s"]="The Engineering Labs are a multi-tiered research and manufacturing facility deep within Gnomeregan. Connected to the Workshop Entrance and Launch Bay, this bustling center of gnome innovation was overrun during the city's radioactive cataclysm and is now swarming with crazed leper gnomes and rogue mechanical contraptions.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Built around a central mechanical structure, the Engineering Labs span two primary tiers connected by a central cargo lift. In Gnomeregan's prime, tinkerers here developed schematics and fine-tuned clockwork inventions. Today, radiation leaks have driven the remaining researchers mad, transforming them into deranged leper gnomes who mindlessly guard malfunctioning machinery alongside rogue constructs.",["t"]="A Fallen Center of Innovation"},{["b"]="Beyond its historical role as a laboratory, the chamber serves as a vital transit hub through the lower reaches of the ruined city. Passages wind toward the Launch Bay, Tinkers' Court, and the Workshop Entrance back door. The lower floor also houses the Matrix Punchograph 3005-D terminals, critical processing units required to decipher the coded punch cards carried by gnome engineers.",["t"]="Crucial Junction"}}}}}
t["subzone:falfarren-river"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,448,28.563.0,23.395.0,45.261.0,63.255.0,58.267.0",["h"]="7d5665",["n"]="Río Falfarren",["s"]="Río Falfarren. El Río Falfarren fluye de noreste a suroeste por el corazón de Vallefresno; nace en las laderas del Monte Hyjal antes de deslizarse bajo tierra bajo las montañas del norte de Los Baldíos. Forma una frontera natural entre los dominios de los elfos de la noche alrededor de Astranaar, al oeste, y las avanzadas invasoras de la Horda, al este. Los viajeros deben andar con cautela, pues sus orillas sombrías y sus aguas poco profundas albergan fauna hostil y marcan el límite del conflicto abierto. Descendiendo desde el Monte Hyjal, las aguas del Falfarren caen en cascadas hacia Xavian antes de serpentear entre el Puesto del Hachazo y la Senda de la Noche. Aunque no es excepcionalmente profundo ni intransitable en condiciones climáticas normales, sirve como la línea divisoria geopolítica aproximada en el centro de Vallefresno. Al oeste se encuentran Astranaar y las posesiones principales de los Kaldorei; al este se asientan los campamentos y las operaciones madereras de la Horda. Cruzar los puentes de madera del camino principal lleva a los viajeros al disputado corazón del bosque, donde las patrullas se enfrentan a lo largo de las orillas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Night Elves and their allies, crossing eastward over the Falfarren signifies stepping directly into the Horde's front lines near Splintertree Post.",["faction:Horde"]="The Falfarren marks the western edge of the Horde's expansion out of Splintertree Post, beyond which lies fortified night elf territory."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Falfarren River starts in the heights of Mount Hyjal, cascading down waterfalls into the lake at Xavian. From there, it meanders southwest across Ashenvale before plunging underground into subterranean channels beneath the northern mountains of the Barrens.",["al"]={"falfarren river source","where does the river go"},["q"]="Where does the Falfarren River begin and end?"},{["a"]="It serves as the rough borderline between night elf and Horde control in central Ashenvale. Night elf territory, centered around Astranaar, lies to the west, while the orc outpost of Splintertree Post and active Horde lumbering operations lie to the east.",["al"]={"why is falfarren river important","river border ashenvale"},["q"]="Why is the Falfarren River significant to the war in Ashenvale?"},{["a"]="Aggressive bog beasts roam the shallows, particularly near the corrupted regions around Felfire Hill. In addition, patrols from both the Alliance and the Horde watch the bridges and crossings, making unattended river banks prime territory for skirmishes and ambushes.",["al"]={"monsters in falfarren river","dangers at falfarren"},["q"]="What threats should travelers expect along the riverbanks?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale river","astranaar","falfarren","falfarren river","felfire hill","splintertree","xavian"},["n"]="Falfarren River",["s"]="The Falfarren River flows northeast to southwest through the heart of Ashenvale, originating on the slopes of Mount Hyjal before slipping underground beneath the Barrens' northern mountains. It forms a natural boundary between night elven domains around Astranaar to the west and the encroaching Horde outposts to the east. Travelers must tread carefully, as its shaded banks and shallows harbor hostile wildlife and mark the edge of open conflict.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Feeding down from Mount Hyjal, the waters of the Falfarren cascade across waterfalls into Xavian before winding between Splintertree Post and Night Run. While it is neither exceptionally deep nor impassable under ordinary weather, it serves as the rough geopolitical dividing line in central Ashenvale. To the west lie Astranaar and the core holdings of the Kaldorei; to the east sit the camps and lumber operations of the Horde. Crossing the main road's wooden bridges brings travelers into the contested heart of the forest, where patrols clash along the banks.",["t"]="A Contested Natural Boundary"},{["b"]="Beyond the tensions of warring sentinels and grunts, the river conceals natural and unnatural dangers beneath its surface. Downstream near Felfire Hill, corrupted bog beasts and aggressive water creatures prowl the muddy shallows. Rainfall can swell the currents, yet the true peril lies in the dense canopies flanking either shore, where ambushes and skirmishes routinely spill into the stream.",["t"]="Hazards in the Shallows"}}}}}
t["subzone:fallen-sky-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,303,21.568.0,33.153.0,43.170.0,41.228.0",["h"]="7173a8",["n"]="Lago Cielo Estrellado",["s"]="Lago Cielo Estrellado. El Lago Cielo Estrellado es una masa de agua aislada enclavada en las profundidades de los bosques del este de Vallefresno. Situadas entre la Avanzada Ala de Plata y el invasor Campo de trabajos forzados Grito de Guerra, sus serenas aguas ocultan peligro en forma de sombramatorral woodkin hostiles que defienden agresivamente el lago y su isla central. Escondido al sur de la Avanzada Ala de Plata y justo al oeste del Campo de trabajos forzados Grito de Guerra, el Lago Cielo Estrellado ofrece un fugaz vistazo al esplendor natural de Vallefresno antes de que las hachas orcas echaran raíces en las cercanías. Las orillas y el pequeño islote que se alza en medio del lago están habitados por shadethickets: lechúcicos corruptos o territoriales que consideran una amenaza a cualquier intruso bípedo. El corazón de la isla sirve como dominio de un poderoso Oráculo Sombramatorral, cuya presencia mantiene a los woodkin locales vinculados a la arboleda e implacablemente vigilantes contra los viajeros que pasan por allí.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Wildkin are traditionally sacred creatures touched by Elune's grace, making the corrupted, aggressive shadethickets infesting Fallen Sky Lake an unsettling sight to behold.",["race:NightElf"]="Positioned just south of Silverwing Outpost, the lake represents yet another corner of the sacred ancestral forest where wild beasts have grown erratic amidst the gathering drums of the Horde."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Fallen Sky Lake is located in eastern Ashenvale, directly south of Silverwing Outpost, west of the Warsong Labor Camp, and northeast of Silverwing Grove.",["al"]={"fallen sky lake location","where is fallen sky lake","how to find fallen sky lake"},["q"]="Where is Fallen Sky Lake located?"},{["a"]="The lake and its surrounding banks are overrun by shadethickets—aggressive wildkin creatures—led by a formidable Shadethicket Oracle who dwells on the central island.",["al"]={"mobs at fallen sky lake","what is at fallen sky lake","fallen sky lake enemies"},["q"]="What creatures live around Fallen Sky Lake?"},{["a"]="The Shadethicket Oracle is the matriarchal leader of the local woodkin gathered at the lake. Travelers and scouts in Ashenvale are often tasked with hunting down the oracle on her central isle to cull the hostile wildkin threat.",["al"]={"oracle at fallen sky lake","shadethicket oracle","who is on the island"},["q"]="Why is the Shadethicket Oracle important?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","fallen sky lake","oracle","shadethicket","silverwing outpost","warsong labor camp","wildkin"},["n"]="Fallen Sky Lake",["s"]="Fallen Sky Lake is a secluded body of water nestled deep within the forests of eastern Ashenvale. Situated between Silverwing Outpost and the encroaching Warsong Labor Camp, the serene waters hide danger in the form of hostile shadethicket woodkin that aggressively defend the lake and its central isle.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked south of Silverwing Outpost and just west of the Warsong Labor Camp, Fallen Sky Lake offers a fleeting glimpse of Ashenvale's natural splendor before the Orcish axes took root nearby. The shores and the small islet rising from the middle of the lake are inhabited by shadethickets—corrupted or territorial wildkin that view any two-legged intruder as a threat. The heart of the island serves as the domain of a powerful Shadethicket Oracle, whose presence keeps the local woodkin bound to the grove and relentlessly vigilant against travelers passing through.",["t"]="A Contested Sanctuary"}}}}}
t["subzone:faol-s-rest"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,371,22.547.0,41.541.0,21.325.0,56.301.0,37.280.0,60.263.0",["h"]="62d7a7",["n"]="Tumba de Faol",["s"]="Tumba de Faol. La Tumba de Faol es un sepulcro tranquilo y descuidado situado en el este de los Claros de Tirisfal, justo al suroeste del Monasterio Escarlata. Se erigió como la tumba del arzobispo Alonsus Faol, el venerado patriarca espiritual que fundó los Caballeros de la Mano de Plata. Hoy en día, descuidada bajo la bóveda arbórea asolada por la plaga, sirve como cementerio de reaparición para quienes perecen cerca del monasterio. Antes de que la Tercera Guerra devastara Lordaeron, esta vaguada apartada era un lugar de solemne peregrinaje. Alberga la tumba de piedra del arzobispo Alonsus Faol, quien guio a la Iglesia de la Luz Sagrada a través de los oscuros días de la Segunda Guerra e instituyó la orden de paladines para proteger a la humanidad. Faol falleció en paz antes de la llegada de la Plaga, librándose de la agonía mortal de ver caer su reino. En aquellos años más luminosos, los dolientes recorrían regularmente el camino desde la capital de Lordaeron para dejar ofrendas y rendir homenaje al querido patriarca.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Every paladin owes their calling to Archbishop Faol, who first gathered Uther and his peers to unite the martial arts with the Holy Light. Standing before his untended tomb is a sobering reminder of the order's beginnings.",["class:Priest"]="As the supreme leader of the Church of the Holy Light through the Second War, Faol was the shepherd of all priesthoods in Lordaeron; seeing his monument ruined reflects the church's tragic ruin in the north."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Alonsus Faol was the Archbishop of the Church of the Holy Light during the Second War. Revered for his wisdom and compassion, he organized relief for refugees and founded the Knights of the Silver Hand, transforming holy priests and pious knights into humanity's first paladins, including Uther the Lightbringer and Turalyon.",["al"]={"who is faol","alonsus faol lore","who is buried here"},["q"]="Who was Alonsus Faol?"},{["a"]="The grounds near the Scarlet Monastery were historically significant religious holdings of the Church of the Holy Light in northern Lordaeron. Faol was laid to rest in this tranquil corner of Tirisfal Glades before the kingdom fell, long before the scarlet-clad zealots fortified the nearby monastery.",["al"]={"why near monastery","scarlet monastery connection","location meaning"},["q"]="Why is this monument located near the Scarlet Monastery?"},{["a"]="No. Since the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge, the site has been utterly neglected. The Scarlet Crusade rarely descends into the hollow to tend it, and the Forsaken have little interest in honoring the shrines of the old church, leaving the stone markers weathered and overgrown.",["al"]={"who tends faol's rest","is it abandoned","tomb upkeep"},["q"]="Is anyone maintaining the tomb today?"},{["a"]="Faol's Rest functions as the local spirit graveyard for the surrounding wilderness and the Scarlet Monastery. Adventurers who perish attempting to breach the monastery or traversing eastern Tirisfal find their spirits returning to the Archbishop's quiet monument.",["al"]={"graveyard run","what is this place in game","monastery graveyard"},["q"]="What practical purpose does Faol's Rest serve for travelers?"}},["kw"]={"alonsus faol","church of the holy light","faol's rest","graveyard","scarlet monastery","silver hand","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Faol's Rest",["s"]="Faol's Rest is a quiet, neglected gravesite situated in eastern Tirisfal Glades, just southwest of the Scarlet Monastery. It was erected as the tomb of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, the revered spiritual patriarch who founded the Knights of the Silver Hand. Today, untended beneath the blighted canopy, it serves as a release graveyard for those who perish near the monastery.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, this secluded hollow was a place of solemn pilgrimage. It holds the stone tomb of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, who led the Church of the Holy Light through the dark days of the Second War and instituted the order of paladins to protect humanity. Faol passed away peacefully prior to the arrival of the Scourge, spared the mortal agony of seeing his kingdom fall. In those brighter years, mourners regularly journeyed up the road from Capital City to leave offerings and pay respects to the beloved patriarch.",["t"]="Tomb of the Archbishop"},{["b"]="When the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron, Tirisfal withered, and the pilgrims vanished. Today, the monument sits abandoned and cracked in the shadows beneath the Scarlet Monastery's high bluffs. The wild brush has reclaimed the pathways, and the tomb itself lies still amid the damp mist. For adventurers striving against the zealots of the Scarlet Crusade or the lingering terrors of Tirisfal, this forgotten resting place now serves primarily as a quiet threshold where fallen spirits briefly regroup before returning to the fray.",["t"]="Desolation in the Shadow of the Monastery"}}}}}
t["subzone:far-watch-post"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,293,22.683.0,38.265.0,26.175.0,35.233.0",["h"]="f11597",["n"]="Avanzada del Puente",["s"]="Avanzada del Puente. La Avanzada del Puente es un puesto avanzado fortificado de la Horda situado justo al oeste del puente sobre el Río Furia del Sur que conecta Durotar con Los Baldíos. Al servir como primera línea de defensa del territorio orco, el puesto protege caravanas comerciales vitales contra agresivas manadas de jabaespines y las hostiles incursiones de la Alianza. Situada al pie occidental del puente que sale de Durotar, la Avanzada del Puente es el primer bastión de la autoridad de la Horda que ven los viajeros al entrar en la vasta y árida sabana de Los Baldíos. El asentamiento es espartano pero funcional, construido para la preparación táctica más que para el confort. Cuenta con una robusta torre de vigilancia orca, un cubil y catapultas de asedio ya calibradas y orientadas hacia las polvorientas llanuras. Justo al sur del camino principal, los peones cuidan un corral de lobos de monta listos para transportar mensajeros o refuerzos. La Avanzada del Puente existe principalmente para mantener segura la ruta de suministros hacia El Cruce, inspeccionando el tráfico entrante y repeliendo los asaltos de las tribus errantes de jabaespines y de los sigilosos exploradores de la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Positioned squarely across the bridge from Durotar, Far Watch Post stands as a formidable roadblock that prevents scouting parties and saboteurs from easily approaching the orcish capital.",["faction:Horde"]="For young warriors stepping out of Durotar for the first time, Far Watch Post is the final outpost of familiar ground before venturing into the rugged, dangerous heartland of Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The post acts as the primary border station between Durotar and the Barrens. Its defenders protect vital Horde supply caravans and ensure that local dangers, notably aggressive quilboar tribes and Alliance trespassers, do not cross the Southfury River into Durotar.",["al"]={"why is far watch post here","purpose of far watch","far watch outpost role"},["q"]="What is the purpose of Far Watch Post?"},{["a"]="Far Watch Post is an active military encampment manned by the Horde. Orc grunts garrison the tower and maintain the siege engines, supported by peons overseeing riding wolves.",["al"]={"who runs far watch post","far watch post faction"},["q"]="Who controls this outpost?"},{["a"]="The post faces frequent harassment from nearby quilboar packs that contest the surrounding thorn-covered scrubland. It also stands on guard against Alliance incursions that might attempt to strike across the Barrens toward Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"far watch post enemies","dangers at far watch"},["q"]="What threats does the outpost face?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","burrow","durotar","far watch post","peons","quilboar","southfury river","watchtower","wolves"},["n"]="Far Watch Post",["s"]="Far Watch Post is a fortified Horde outpost situated just west of the Southfury River bridge connecting Durotar to the Barrens. Serving as the front line of defense for the orcish homeland, the post guards vital trade caravans against aggressive quilboar packs and hostile Alliance incursions.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located at the western foot of the bridge out of Durotar, Far Watch Post is the first bastion of Horde authority travellers see when entering the vast, arid savannah of the Barrens. The settlement is Spartan but functional, built for tactical readiness rather than comfort. It features a sturdy orcish watchtower, a burrow, and pre-sighted siege catapults trained toward the dusty plains. Directly south of the main road, peons tend a pen of riding wolves ready to bear messengers or reinforcements. Far Watch Post exists primarily to keep the supply road to Crossroads secure, screening incoming traffic and repelling raids from roaming quilboar tribes and stealthy Alliance scouts.",["t"]="Guardian of the Border"}}}}}
t["subzone:fargodeep-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,222,11.492.0,20.361.0,41.252.0,55.222.0,17.171.0,52.251.0",["h"]="cb0fdf",["n"]="Mina Abisal",["s"]="Mina Abisal. Mina Abisal es una mina de oro abandonada situada en el centro del Bosque de Elwynn, al sur de Villadorada. Antaño una productiva fuente de riqueza para el Reino de Ventormenta, hace poco ha sido invadida por un clan beligerante de kóbolds. Mina Abisal proporcionaba antes un flujo constante de oro al tesoro de Ventormenta, pero la menguante presencia militar del reino en Elwynn ha dejado vulnerables los recursos periféricos. Los kóbolds no tardaron en abarrotar los oscuros túneles, estableciendo una bulliciosa madriguera bajo las colinas. El Alguacil Dughan y las autoridades locales de Villadorada ven la infestación con profunda preocupación, no solo por el mineral perdido, sino porque estas envalentonadas criaturas amenazan ahora granjas cercanas como las tierras de los Stonefield y los Maclure.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing the vermin out of Fargodeep Mine is vital for securing the supply lines and farmlands immediately surrounding Goldshire.",["profession:Mining"]="Though infested with pests, the rocky tunnels of Fargodeep remain rich in accessible copper veins for fledgling miners."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The mine was neglected as Stormwind's military stretched thin across southern lands. With town guards focused on protecting Goldshire and the main roads, the subterranean dig site was left unguarded, allowing kobolds to move in and fortify the tunnels.",["al"]={"why abandoned","why did humans leave fargodeep","who owned fargodeep mine"},["q"]="Why did Stormwind abandon Fargodeep Mine?"},{["a"]="Fargodeep Mine lies right between the Stonefield and Maclure family farms. The kobolds venture out from the tunnels to steal livestock, tools, and personal belongings, harassing anyone who wanders near the mine's entrance.",["al"]={"why are kobolds a problem","kobold threat","stonefield kobolds"},["q"]="Why are the kobolds here so dangerous to local farmers?"},{["a"]="Goldtooth is a prominent kobold who nests deep within the lower shafts of Fargodeep Mine. He is notorious for snatching Auntie Bernice Stonefield's prized family necklace.",["al"]={"goldtooth","who is goldtooth","goldtooth location"},["q"]="Who is Goldtooth?"},{["a"]="Local merchants and townsfolk see opportunity in clearing the pests: Remy 'Two Times' buys up salvaged gold dust, the alchemist William Pestle uses kobold candle wax for reagents, and Marshal Dughan needs the infestation monitored to safeguard Elwynn.",["al"]={"fargodeep quests","why gather candles","gold dust"},["q"]="Why do people in Goldshire want items from the mine?"}},["kw"]={"candles","elwynn","fargodeep","fargodeep mine","goldshire","goldtooth","kobold","marshal dughan","remy two times"},["n"]="Fargodeep Mine",["s"]="Fargodeep Mine is an abandoned gold mine nestled in central Elwynn Forest, south of Goldshire. Once a productive source of wealth for the Kingdom of Stormwind, it has recently been overrun by a belligerent clan of kobolds.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Fargodeep Mine once provided steady gold to Stormwind's treasury, but the Kingdom's dwindling military presence in Elwynn has left outlying resources vulnerable. Kobolds quickly swarmed into the dark tunnels, establishing a bustling warren beneath the hills. Marshal Dughan and the local authorities in Goldshire view the infestation with deep concern, not only because of lost ore, but because the emboldened creatures now threaten nearby farmsteads like the Stonefield and Maclure holdings.",["t"]="A Lost Vein"},{["b"]="The mine spans multiple levels, with the lower shafts winding deep beneath the forest floor. Kobold laborers and vermin scurry along the wooden scaffolds, fiercely guarding their scavenged wax and gold dust. Deeper within lurks Goldtooth, a particularly cunning kobold leader known for hoarding trinkets pilfered from unwary travelers and surrounding residents.",["t"]="Depths of the Warren"}}}}}
t["subzone:farstrider-lodge"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,291,31.554.0,26.459.0,42.216.0,39.205.0,48.177.0",["h"]="321e3a",["n"]="Cabaña del Errante",["s"]="Cabaña del Errante. Escondida en las colinas surorientales de Loch Modan, Cabaña del Errante es un tranquilo puesto de caza construido al estilo de los altos elfos. Aunque se fundó como una parada elfa, hoy en día presta servicio a viajeros, forestales y tramperos de todas las razas de la Alianza que buscan poner a prueba sus habilidades contra la fauna local. Cabaña del Errante se distingue de las robustas obras de piedra y madera típicas de Khaz Modan. Luciendo las elegantes curvas y la carpintería abovedada propias de la artesanía de los altos elfos, el puesto lleva el nombre de los Farstriders, los célebres forestales de Quel'Thalas. Mucho antes de que las guerras recientes devastaran el hogar de los elfos, los Farstriders se desplazaban mucho más al sur de sus fronteras para explorar y estrechar lazos con el resto del mundo. Aunque hoy en día solo un solitario alto elfo permanece para atender la cabaña, su legado de caza perdura bajo la custodia de los enanos y montaraces humanos locales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Farstrider Lodge is a prime sanctuary for hunters, offering both mentorship in marksmanship and beast training amidst the rich game of Loch Modan's surrounding hills.",["race:Dwarf"]="Though built by elven hands, the lodge operates in close harmony with the mountaineers of Thelsamar to monitor the dangerous wildlife threatening Khaz Modan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Farstrider Lodge was established long before the recent wars by the Farstriders, the ranger corps of Quel'Thalas, who sought to maintain a presence and build ties across the wider world beyond their northern kingdom.",["al"]={"why elven building loch modan","who built farstrider lodge","why high elf lodge here"},["q"]="Why is there an elven lodge in Khaz Modan?"},{["a"]="Only a single high elf, the innkeeper Vyrin Swiftwind, currently resides at the lodge. The rest of the occupants are dwarven mountaineers and human huntsmen who maintain the lodge and trade with travelers.",["al"]={"are there high elves here","who lives in farstrider lodge","vyrin swiftwind"},["q"]="Are there still high elves living here?"},{["a"]="The lodge primarily supports outdoorsmen, providing a hunter trainer, a pet trainer, local merchants, and rest for wilderness scouts tracking dangerous wildlife across the loch.",["al"]={"what is at farstrider lodge","hunter trainers loch modan"},["q"]="What services are available at Farstrider Lodge?"}},["kw"]={"farstrider lodge","farstriders","high elf","hunter lodge","loch modan","thelsamar","vyrin swiftwind"},["n"]="Farstrider Lodge",["s"]="Tucked away in the southeastern hills of Loch Modan, Farstrider Lodge is a tranquil hunting outpost built in high elven style. Though founded as an elven waystation, it now serves travelers, rangers, and trappers of all Alliance races looking to test their skills against the local wildlife.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Farstrider Lodge stands apart from the sturdy stone and timber works typical of Khaz Modan. Bearing the graceful curves and vaulted woodwork of high elven craftsmanship, the outpost is named after the Farstriders, the renowned rangers of Quel'Thalas. Long before the recent wars shattered the elven homeland, Farstriders ranged far south of their borders to explore and build ties with the wider world. While only a solitary high elf remains to tend the lodge today, its hunting heritage endures under the stewardship of local dwarves and human woodsmen.",["t"]="An Elven Haven in the Mountains"},{["b"]="Situated high on the bluffs overlooking the loch, the lodge serves as a base of operations for hunters, scouts, and trappers navigating the untamed corners of the zone. Between offering training for marksmen and shelter from roaming beasts, the lodge remains closely tied to the nearby settlement of Thelsamar, ensuring that supplies and wilderness intelligence flow freely between the dwarven mountaineers and the woodsmen guarding the southeastern frontier.",["t"]="A Waystation for the Wilds"}}}}}
t["subzone:fel-rock"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,238,19.354.0,16.468.0,26.110.0,19.133.0,40.244.0,39.111.0",["h"]="d45883",["n"]="Roca Mácula",["s"]="Roca Mácula. Roca Mácula es una caverna asolada oculta en los bosques justo al norte de Dolanaar, sobre las ramas de Teldrassil. En el pasado fue una hondonada tranquila, pero ha caído en la corrupción bajo la influencia del sátiro Lord Melenas y su horda de viles grells. Escondida en las colinas boscosas al norte de Dolanaar, Roca Mácula fue antaño una caverna ordinaria y apacible excavada en la madera y la piedra de Teldrassil. Hoy en día, se alza como un inquietante recordatorio de la corrupción invasora que amenaza al Árbol del Mundo. Raíces retorcidas y sombras antinaturales dominan el interior de la caverna, infestada por enjambres de grells salvajes y parientes de grell.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Cenarion Circle view Fel Rock as a festering wound on the young world tree, requiring immediate purging before demonic corruption spreads.",["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the presence of a satyr like Lord Melenas so close to Dolanaar is an alarming affront to Teldrassil that demands swift retribution."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Fel Rock is located in central Teldrassil, tucked into the hills directly north of the settlement of Dolanaar.",["al"]={"fel rock location","where is fel rock","find fel rock"},["q"]="Where is Fel Rock located?"},{["a"]="The cavern is commanded by Lord Melenas, a vile satyr who has made Fel Rock his lair and gathered a host of grells to do his bidding.",["al"]={"who is in fel rock","boss of fel rock","lord melenas location"},["q"]="Who rules Fel Rock?"},{["a"]="The presence of a satyr and fel-tainted grells within the world tree's boughs poses an immediate threat to the natural balance of Teldrassil. Druids like Tallonkai Swiftroot dispatch adventurers to cut down Lord Melenas and stem the corruption.",["al"]={"why clean fel rock","fel rock quest","tallonkai swiftroot quest"},["q"]="Why are druids concerned about Fel Rock?"},{["a"]="Inside Fel Rock, you will encounter aggressive grells, grellkin, and their dark master, the satyr Lord Melenas.",["al"]={"fel rock mobs","what is inside fel rock","fel rock enemies"},["q"]="What creatures dwell inside the cavern?"}},["kw"]={"dolanaar","fel rock","grell","lord melenas","satyr","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil"},["n"]="Fel Rock",["s"]="Fel Rock is a blighted cavern hidden within the woods just north of Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil. Once a tranquil hollow, it has fallen into corruption under the influence of the satyr Lord Melenas and his horde of vicious grells.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the forested hills north of Dolanaar, Fel Rock was once an ordinary, peaceful cavern carved into the wood and stone of Teldrassil. Today, it stands as an unsettling reminder of the creeping taint encroaching on the world tree. Twisted roots and unnatural shadows dominate the cavern interior, overrun by swarms of wild grells and grellkin.",["t"]="A Den of Corruption"},{["b"]="The corruption within Fel Rock stems from the presence of Lord Melenas, a wicked satyr who has claimed the hollow as a stronghold. From deep within the cave, he orchestrates the spread of malevolent corruption right under the watchful gaze of the night elf sentinels. Druids from Dolanaar, particularly Tallonkai Swiftroot, actively enlist capable defenders to cleanse the cave and slay Melenas before his foul blight can spread further into the surrounding woodlands.",["t"]="The Satyr's Hold"}}}}}
t["subzone:felfire-hill"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,296,28.418.0,22.387.0,30.264.0,36.201.0,43.238.0,45.262.0",["h"]="4dcf66",["n"]="Cerro Lumbrevil",["s"]="Cerro Lumbrevil. Cerro Lumbrevil es una colina marchita e infestada de demonios ubicada en el este de Vallefresno. Azotada por la caída de infernales durante la Tercera Guerra, su tierra corrupta aún arde con poder demoníaco. La Horda mantiene puestos de guardia fortificados en los puentes que conducen a la colina para proteger sus asentamientos cercanos. Durante la invasión cataclísmica de la Tercera Guerra, cayeron meteoros llameantes por todo Kalimdor mientras la Legión Ardiente desataba a sus temibles infernales. Varios de esos colosos ardientes se estrellaron contra esta cresta en Vallefresno, arrasando los bosques ancestrales y corrompiendo la propia tierra. Hoy en día, el paisaje abrasado sigue saturado de energía vil y acechado por demonios rezagados que sobrevivieron a la derrota de la Legión en el Monte Hyjal.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="The raw fel energies lingering where the Legion's infernals made landfall make this scarred ridge an object of dangerous curiosity for practitioners of dark magic.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde holds the fortified bridges around Felfire Hill to safeguard the transit road connecting Splintertree Post with the Warsong Lumber Camp against demonic raids."},["faq"]={{["a"]="During the Third War, Burning Legion infernals rained down from the sky and slammed into this hill. The impact and subsequent fel contamination burned away the pristine elven forest, leaving behind scarred rock and corrupting demonic energies that never dispersed.",["al"]={"why is felfire hill green","felfire hill lore","what happened to felfire hill"},["q"]="Why is Felfire Hill corrupted?"},{["a"]="The hill is occupied by surviving demons and infernal constructs left over from the Legion's invasion during the Third War. They remain hostile to all mortals who wander near their corrupted perimeter.",["al"]={"monsters at felfire hill","felfire hill mobs"},["q"]="What creatures live on Felfire Hill?"},{["a"]="Felfire Hill lies directly between Splintertree Post and the Warsong Lumber Camp. Horde commanders fortified both bridges to ensure the roaming demons cannot break out and overrun their nearby camps, supply convoys, and lumber operations.",["al"]={"horde bridge guards felfire","why are orcs guarding felfire hill"},["q"]="Why did the Horde fortify the bridges here?"},{["a"]="Though the hill itself was once part of Ashenvale's sacred forest, it now sits menacingly northeast of the Dor'Danil Barrow Den. The creeping demonic taint and roaming fiends pose an enduring danger to the nearby slumbering grounds and the surrounding wildlands.",["al"]={"dor danil felfire hill","barrow den demons"},["q"]="Is Felfire Hill connected to the night elves?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","burning legion","demons","felfire hill","infernals","splintertree post","warsong lumber camp"},["n"]="Felfire Hill",["s"]="Felfire Hill is a blighted, demon-infested rise nestled in eastern Ashenvale. Struck by falling infernals during the Third War, its corrupted soil still burns with demonic power. The Horde maintains fortified guard posts on the bridges leading into the hill to safeguard their nearby settlements.",["sec"]={{["b"]="During the cataclysmic invasion of the Third War, flaming meteors fell across Kalimdor as the Burning Legion unleashed its dread infernals. Several of those fiery behemoths struck this ridge in Ashenvale, scouring away the ancient woodlands and corrupting the earth itself. Today, the scorched landscape remains saturated with fel energy and prowled by lingering demons who survived the Legion's defeat at Mount Hyjal.",["t"]="A Scar of the Burning Legion"},{["b"]="Situated southeast of Splintertree Post and southwest of the Warsong Lumber Camp, Felfire Hill sits uncomfortably close to vital Horde operations. Because the demonic remnants threaten to spill out into the surrounding forest, Horde forces have erected fortified barricades and guard towers at both bridges approaching the hill, containing the foul creatures within their blighted haven.",["t"]="Guarding the Crossings"}}}}}
t["subzone:fenris-isle"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,266,31.583.0,25.525.1,20.258.0,35.163.0,50.229.0,52.263.0",["h"]="7568d3",["n"]="Isla de Fenris",["s"]="Isla de Fenris. La Isla de Fenris es una gran isla envuelta en niebla situada en el Lago Lordamere, en el límite oriental del Bosque de Argénteos. En el pasado albergó un bullicioso bastión militar de Lordaeron, pero ahora se encuentra bajo el yugo de los gnolls pielpodrida no-muertos y de un nigromante renegado de la Plaga. Antes de que la Tercera Guerra devastara el norte de Lordaeron, la Isla de Fenris sirvió como un puesto de avanzada vital para el reino, protegido por el Castillo de Fenris. Cuando la Plaga arrasó el reino, la guarnición fue masacrada o huyó al exilio, dejando la isla abandonada a los muertos. Con el paso de los años, la isla se convirtió en un baluarte para los gnolls pielpodrida: viles criaturas plagadas que establecieron un rudimentario imperio a lo largo de las orillas del lago. Los Renegados del Bosque de Argénteos vigilan de cerca la isla, pues consideran que sus atrincherados habitantes son una grave amenaza para sus territorios del norte.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers are enlisted by Forsaken commanders to board boats across Lordamere Lake, storm the island's defenses, and assassinate the renegade necromancer orchestrating attacks from Fenris Keep.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Fenris Isle represents an intolerable Scourge bastion in their own backyard, requiring relentless strikes to keep Thule Ravenclaw's rot-hides from overrunning Silverpine's eastern waters."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Fenris Isle is an island located in Lordamere Lake off the eastern coast of Silverpine Forest. Prior to the Third War, it served as a fortress redoubt for the Kingdom of Lordaeron, but it is now infested with plague-ridden gnolls and servants of the Scourge.",["al"]={"where is fenris isle","fenris isle lore","what is this island"},["q"]="What is Fenris Isle?"},{["a"]="The island is occupied by the Rot Hide gnolls under the command of Thule Ravenclaw, a rogue necromancer aligned with the Scourge who directs them from Fenris Keep.",["al"]={"who runs fenris isle","fenris isle bosses","who lives on fenris isle"},["q"]="Who controls Fenris Isle right now?"},{["a"]="During the Third War, the human defenders and inhabitants of Fenris Keep were either murdered or driven away as the Scourge overran Lordaeron. The fortress was left ruined until gnolls and necromancers claimed the empty ramparts.",["al"]={"what happened to fenris keep humans","who built fenris keep"},["q"]="What happened to the humans who used to live here?"},{["a"]="The Forsaken consider the entrenched Scourge forces and Rot Hide gnolls on Fenris Isle an active security threat to their holdings in Silverpine Forest. The Horde launches incursions across Lordamere Lake to eliminate Thule Ravenclaw and dismantle his operations.",["al"]={"assault on fenris isle lore","why do horde attack fenris isle","forsaken fenris isle"},["q"]="Why is the Horde interested in attacking the island?"}},["kw"]={"fenris isle","fenris keep","lordamere lake","rot hide","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},["n"]="Fenris Isle",["s"]="Fenris Isle is a large, mist-shrouded island in Lordamere Lake, bordering the eastern edge of Silverpine Forest. Once home to a bustling Lordaeron military stronghold, the island now lies under the iron grip of undead Rot Hide gnolls and a rogue Scourge necromancer.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War devastated northern Lordaeron, Fenris Isle served as a vital outpost for the kingdom, anchored by Fenris Keep. When the Scourge tore through the realm, the garrison was slaughtered or fled into exile, leaving the island abandoned to the dead. In the years since, the island became a stronghold for the Rot Hide gnolls—vile, plague-ridden creatures who established a crude empire across the lake's shores. The Forsaken of Silverpine Forest keep a vigilant watch on the island, viewing its entrenched inhabitants as a severe threat to their northern territories.",["t"]="A Fallen Stronghold on the Lake"},{["b"]="The Rot Hide gnolls do not act alone. Within the crumbling stone halls of Fenris Keep dwells Thule Ravenclaw, a cunning necromancer formerly aligned with the Kirin Tor who turned to the dark arts of the Scourge. Thule bent the native gnolls to his will, using dark sorcery to animate their fallen kin and fortify the island against intrusion. From this isolated sanctuary, Thule oversees the lake's ferry crossings, prompting Forsaken scouts and Horde forces to launch preemptive strikes to break his hold on the archipelago.",["t"]="The Master of Fenris Keep"}}}}}
t["subzone:fenris-keep"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,235,29.591.0,24.473.1,20.194.0,32.187.0,40.238.0,43.262.0",["h"]="708bd5",["n"]="Castillo de Fenris",["s"]="Castillo de Fenris. El Castillo de Fenris es una fortaleza de piedra aislada situada en lo alto de la Isla de Fenris, en el corazón del Lago Lordamere. Antaño un bastión estratégico que albergaba tropas de Lordaeron, ha caído en manos de la Plaga bajo el mando del mago renegado Thule Corvozarpa. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, el Castillo de Fenris tenía una gran importancia estratégica para el Reino de Lordaeron, albergando un contingente considerable de tropas para proteger el Lago Lordamere. Cuando la Plaga de los no-muertos asoló la región, la fortaleza insular fue arrasada junto con el resto del reino. En lugar de desmoronarse en una ruina olvidada, fue tomada por Thule Corvozarpa, un antiguo mago traidor del Kirin Tor. Corvozarpa se alió con la Plaga, subyugó a los gnolls locales con vil nigromancia para crear la voraz jauría de los Podrepiel y se atrincheró en lo más profundo de las salas de piedra del castillo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="The master of Fenris Keep, Thule Ravenclaw, represents a grim betrayal of the Kirin Tor's teachings, having twisted Dalaran's arcane knowledge into the dark arts of the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde—and the Forsaken in particular—Fenris Keep represents a lingering Scourge stronghold that must be eradicated to safeguard Silverpine Forest and the waterways of Lordamere Lake."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Fenris Keep is a fortified stone castle situated on Fenris Isle in Lordamere Lake. Formerly a military stronghold for the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron, it is currently held by the undead Scourge.",["al"]={"fenris keep lore","what is fenris keep","fenris castle"},["q"]="What is Fenris Keep?"},{["a"]="The keep is ruled by Thule Ravenclaw, a former Kirin Tor mage who betrayed the living to serve the Scourge. He commands an army of undead-tainted Rot Hide gnolls from within the fortress.",["al"]={"who controls fenris keep","fenris keep boss","master of fenris isle"},["q"]="Who rules Fenris Keep right now?"},{["a"]="The local gnoll population was subjugated by Thule Ravenclaw through dark magic and disease, twisting them into the Rot Hide gnolls. They serve as Ravenclaw's loyal shock troops and guards throughout the castle and the surrounding island.",["al"]={"rot hide gnolls fenris","why gnolls in keep","fenris gnolls"},["q"]="Why are there gnolls inside Fenris Keep?"},{["a"]="Fenris Keep provides the Scourge with a defensible base on Lordamere Lake, directly menacing Forsaken movements through eastern Silverpine Forest and Tirisfal Glades. Sylvanas's forces cannot leave an active Scourge commander unchecked so close to their borders.",["al"]={"why forsaken attack fenris","forsaken fenris keep","undercity fenris"},["q"]="Why do the Forsaken care about Fenris Keep?"}},["kw"]={"fenris isle","fenris keep","lordaeron","lordamere lake","rot hide","scourge","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},["n"]="Fenris Keep",["s"]="Fenris Keep is an isolated stone fortress situated atop Fenris Isle in the heart of Lordamere Lake. Once a strategic stronghold housing Lordaeron troops, it has fallen into the hands of the Scourge under the rogue mage Thule Ravenclaw.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, Fenris Keep held strategic importance for the Kingdom of Lordaeron, stationing a sizable contingent of troops to safeguard Lordamere Lake. When the undead Scourge swept across the land, the island fortress was overwhelmed along with the rest of the realm. Rather than crumbling into forgotten ruin, it was seized by Thule Ravenclaw, a traitorous former wizard of the Kirin Tor. Ravenclaw allied himself with the Scourge, subjugated the resident gnolls with foul necromancy to create the ravenous Rot Hide pack, and entrenched himself deep inside the keep's stone halls.",["t"]="A Fallen Bastion of Lordaeron"},{["b"]="Today, Fenris Keep serves as the seat of Ravenclaw's power and an imminent threat to the Forsaken securing Silverpine Forest. From this bastion, Thule directs legions of Rot Hide gnolls that violently assail anyone daring to set foot on the isle. Because Fenris Isle sits mere miles across the water from the Tirisfal border, the Forsaken of the Sepulcher and Undercity actively dispatch champions to batter down the keep's defenses and put an end to the rogue necromancer.",["t"]="The Scourge on Lordamere"}}}}}
t["subzone:field-of-giants"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,307,28.517.0,18.478.0,37.206.0,40.231.0,35.247.0,49.253.0",["h"]="dc3ff2",["n"]="Tierra de Gigantes",["s"]="Tierra de Gigantes. La Tierra de Gigantes es una extensa llanura que cubre el sur de Los Baldíos entre el Campamento Taurajo y las ciénagas del Marjal Revolcafango. Bautizada así por los imponentes kodos, lagartos del trueno y enormes bestias que pastan en sus áridos matorrales, la región se ha vuelto recientemente mucho más peligrosa debido a una creciente plaga de silítidos. Extendiéndose a lo largo del tramo sur del Camino del Oro, la Tierra de Gigantes es remota, escarpada y apenas está defendida en comparación con Los Baldíos del norte. Aunque las atalayas de madera del camino se encuentran prácticamente abandonadas, la propia tierra rebosa vida. Enormes manadas de la megafauna de Kalimdor deambulan por las vastas llanuras, atrayendo tanto a cazadores como a naturalistas. Sin embargo, la seguridad es esquiva aquí: los excavadores enanos de Bael Modan cavan agresivamente hacia el sur, y una amenaza mucho más siniestra ha comenzado a excavar bajo la tierra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The roaming herds of thunder lizards and massive kodo make the Field of Giants one of the premier hunting grounds in the Barrens for those seeking formidable beasts.",["faction:Horde"]="The emergence of silithid hives so close to the road between Camp Taurajo and Dustwallow Marsh threatens travel lines, prompting leaders across the Barrens to call for scouts."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The plain earns its name from the sheer scale of the wildlife roaming it. Great herds of towering kodo beasts and thunder lizards graze here, dominating the landscape alongside massive Kalimdorean wildlife.",["al"]={"field of giants name origin","why field of giants"},["q"]="Why is it called the Field of Giants?"},{["a"]="Those are silithid mounds. These insectoid predators have tunneled up from deep underground, creating the northernmost hives discovered in Kalimdor. Their sudden presence poses a dire threat to passing travelers and local wildlife.",["al"]={"bug mounds barrens","insects in southern barrens","what are the silithid"},["q"]="What are those bug mounds in the ground?"},{["a"]="The plain itself has few settlements, but prominent figures watch its borders. The tauren shaman Brine lives on a southern ridge, while the displaced exile Gann Stonespire watches from nearby, plotting against the dwarven excavation at Bael Modan.",["al"]={"who lives here","field of giants npcs"},["q"]="Who lives near the Field of Giants?"},{["a"]="The Horde's military presence is concentrated heavily along the northern Gold Road around the Crossroads. The southernmost reaches receive far fewer patrols, leaving these towers neglected amidst the creeping threats of silithid and aggressive wildlife.",["al"]={"abandoned towers gold road","southern barrens watchtowers"},["q"]="Why are the watchtowers along the road abandoned?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","camp taurajo","field of giants","gold road","kodo","korran","ruga ragetotem","silithid","thunder lizard"},["n"]="Field of Giants",["s"]="The Field of Giants is an expansive plain covering the southern Barrens between Camp Taurajo and the marshes of Dustwallow. Named for the towering kodo, thunder lizards, and massive beasts that graze its arid scrub, the region has recently grown far more perilous due to an encroaching silithid infestation.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching along the southern span of the Gold Road, the Field of Giants is remote, rugged, and lightly defended compared to the Barrens to the north. While the road's wooden watchtowers stand largely abandoned, the land itself thrums with life. Tremendous herds of Kalimdor's megafauna wander the vast flats, drawing hunters and naturalists alike. However, safety is elusive here: dwarven excavators from Bael Modan dig aggressively to the south, and a far more sinister menace has begun burrowing beneath the earth.",["t"]="A Wild Frontier in the South"},{["b"]="In recent times, insectoid silithid hives have erupted from the ground across the Field of Giants, marking the northernmost known sighting of these ravenous creatures in Kalimdor. These strange mounds and aggressive swarms have alarmed the Horde. Scouts such as the troll Korran from the Crossroads and tauren warriors like Ruga Ragetotem at Camp Taurajo urge adventurers to probe the hives, seeking to uncover what draws these subterranean horrors so far from the deep deserts.",["t"]="The Creeping Swarm"}}}}}
t["subzone:fire-scar-shrine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,241,22.447.0,26.372.0,34.181.0,41.238.0,16.163.0,68.226.0",["h"]="8eda51",["n"]="Santuario de la Escara",["s"]="Santuario de la Escara. El Santuario de la Escara es un santuario de los elfos de la noche profanado, enclavado en los bosques del suroeste de Vallefresno. Antaño un sereno lugar de culto, ha sido corrompido por fuerzas demoníacas y transformado en una ampolla de energía vil a las mismas puertas de Astranaar. Situado al suroeste de Astranaar y al oeste de Las ruinas del Polvo Estelar, el Santuario de la Escara se erige como un lúgubre recordatorio del veneno persistente de la Legión Ardiente en Vallefresno. El santuario ha sucumbido a la corrupción demoníaca, alimentada por los siervos del sombrío Culto de la Facción Oscura y el Consejo de la Sombra. La magia vil ha retorcido la tierra circundante convirtiéndola en roca calcinada, donde demonios errantes se reúnen ahora en abierto desafío a los defensores del bosque.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="The fel scarring and wild demonic summons here bear the clear signature of the Shadow Council's subtle infiltrations throughout Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of Fire Scar Shrine is a bitter affront so near to Astranaar, demanding swift retribution against any demonic trespassers who sully the forest."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Fire Scar Shrine is situated in southwestern Ashenvale, directly southwest of the night elf hub of Astranaar, south of the Shrine of Aessina, and just west of the Ruins of Stardust.",["al"]={"fire scar shrine location","where is fire scar shrine","fire scar shrine map"},["q"]="Where is Fire Scar Shrine located?"},{["a"]="The shrine was infiltrated and corrupted by agents of the Shadow Council and the Cult of the Dark Strand, notably the orc warlock Ilkrud Magthrull. Their dark rituals summoned demons and infused the sacred ground with lingering fel taint.",["al"]={"why demons here","what corrupted fire scar shrine","who summoned the demons"},["q"]="Why are there demons at Fire Scar Shrine?"},{["a"]="Akkrilus is a formidable doomguard that occasionally manifests around Fire Scar Shrine, drawn to the potent demonic energies that pool around the corrupted stones.",["al"]={"akkrilus","doomguard at fire scar","rare demon fire scar shrine"},["q"]="Who is Akkrilus?"},{["a"]="The orc warlock who operated here, Ilkrud Magthrull, served Athrikus Narassin, the leader of the Cult of the Dark Strand. They leveraged the shrine as a foothold for their demonic summoning and dark ambitions within Ashenvale.",["al"]={"cult of the dark strand fire scar","dark strand connection","athrikus narassin fire scar"},["q"]="What connection does this place have to the Cult of the Dark Strand?"}},["kw"]={"akkrilus","ashenvale","astranaar","athrikus narassin","cult of the dark strand","fire scar shrine","ilkrud magthrull","shadow council"},["n"]="Fire Scar Shrine",["s"]="Fire Scar Shrine is a despoiled night elf shrine nestled in the southwestern forests of Ashenvale. Once a serene place of worship, it has been corrupted by demonic forces and turned into a blister of fel energy right on Astranaar's doorstep.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located southwest of Astranaar and west of the Ruins of Stardust, Fire Scar Shrine stands as a grim reminder of the Burning Legion's lingering poison in Ashenvale. The shrine has fallen under the sway of demonic corruption, nurtured by servants of the shadowy Cult of the Dark Strand and the Shadow Council. Fel magic has twisted the surrounding earth into scorched rock, where roaming demons now gather in open defiance of the forest's defenders.",["t"]="A Blight in the Forest"},{["b"]="The shrine's descent into darkness was spearheaded by agents like the orcish warlock Ilkrud Magthrull, operating under the orders of Athrikus Narassin. Though mortal sorcerers brought the corruption to bear, summoned fiends now patrol the altar stones unchecked. The localized tear in the veil occasionally draws greater horrors, including the towering doomguard Akkrilus.",["t"]="Shadows of the Dark Strand"}}}}}
t["subzone:forest-s-edge"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,287,20.464.0,19.341.0,31.181.0,30.221.0,14.212.0,47.232.0",["h"]="71be6d",["n"]="Linde del bosque",["s"]="Linde del bosque. Linde del bosque es una cuña boscosa de tierra a lo largo de la frontera suroeste de Bosque de Elwynn, flanqueada por ríos que conducen hacia Páramos de Poniente. Custodiada al norte por Cuartel Arroyoeste, esta zona salvaje ha sido peligrosamente invadida por gnolls zarparrío bajo el mando del infame Hogger. Ubicada al suroeste de Ciudad de Ventormenta, entre Vergel del Lago Espejo y los ríos que bordean Páramos de Poniente, Linde del bosque forma una península natural de bosque. A pesar de su proximidad a Cuartel Arroyoeste, las mermadas filas del ejército de Ventormenta han dejado la zona vulnerable a bestias salvajes y partidas de saqueadores. Jabalíes errantes merodean entre los árboles y a lo largo de las orillas del río, pero la verdadera amenaza es la concentración de gnolls zarparrío que han convertido estos bosques en su base de operaciones.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For recruits stationed in Elwynn Forest, clearing Forest's Edge and defeating Hogger is one of the first major trials proving their combat readiness to the crown.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The quiet riverbanks and shaded groves of Forest's Edge yield common woodland herbs, though gathering them often requires dodging aggressive gnoll patrols."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Forest's Edge is located in the southwestern corner of Elwynn Forest. It sits south of Westbrook Garrison, bordered by Mirror Lake Orchard and the waterways that lead into Westfall.",["al"]={"forests edge location","where is forests edge","forest edge map"},["q"]="Where exactly is Forest's Edge?"},{["a"]="A large and aggressive pack of Riverpaw gnolls has claimed the woods, threatening travel along the southwestern border. The biggest threat is their chieftain, Hogger, an exceptionally vicious gnoll who prowls these woods.",["al"]={"why dangerous forests edge","what is at forest edge","forests edge threats"},["q"]="Why is this area so dangerous?"},{["a"]="Hogger is a notorious, powerful gnoll leader responsible for violent attacks on Elwynn's borders. The Stormwind Army has posted a generous bounty for proof of his death, warning adventurers not to face him alone.",["al"]={"hogger lore","who is hogger","hogger info"},["q"]="Who is Hogger?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's military is stretched remarkably thin across the kingdom. With unrest in Westfall and threats encroaching on all sides, the garrison lacks the manpower to clear the gnoll camps, leaving the task to volunteer adventurers.",["al"]={"why westbrook garrison not clearing","why stormwind guards not help","westbrook guards"},["q"]="Why hasn't Westbrook Garrison cleared the area?"}},["kw"]={"elwynn forest","forest's edge","forests edge","gnolls","hogger","nazferiti river","riverpaw","westbrook garrison"},["n"]="Forest's Edge",["s"]="Forest's Edge is a wooded wedge of land along the southwestern frontier of Elwynn Forest, flanked by rivers leading toward Westfall. Guarded to the north by Westbrook Garrison, this untamed area has become dangerously overrun by riverpaw gnolls under the command of the notorious Hogger.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked southwest of Stormwind City between Mirror Lake Orchard and the rivers bordering Westfall, Forest's Edge forms a natural peninsula of woodland. Despite its proximity to Westbrook Garrison, the Stormwind army's thin ranks have left the area vulnerable to wild beasts and raiding parties. Wandering boars roam among the trees and along the riverbanks, but the true menace is the concentration of Riverpaw gnolls who have made these woods their staging ground.",["t"]="A Contested Frontier"},{["b"]="The woods of Forest's Edge are the hunting grounds of Hogger, a massive and brutal gnoll chieftain. With a sizable bounty placed on his head by the Stormwind Army, Hogger directs his pack in harassing travelers and raiding nearby farms, turning what could be a peaceful timberland into a lethal proving ground for young Alliance adventurers.",["t"]="Hogger's Stronghold"}}}}}
t["subzone:forest-song"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,297,35.537.0,21.515.0,25.126.0,34.252.0,40.197.0,43.177.0",["h"]="92ef37",["n"]="Canción del Bosque",["s"]="Canción del Bosque. Canción del Bosque es una antigua ruina de los elfos de la noche ubicada en el noreste de Vallefresno, cerca de los bosques corruptos de Satyrnaar y del gran portal de Talloumbrío. En la actualidad, se encuentra prácticamente desierta, a excepción del vigilante druida Kayneth Ventoleve, quien custodia la frontera oriental frente a las amenazas emergentes. Escondida en los densos bosques del noreste de Vallefresno, Canción del Bosque fue antaño un elegante asentamiento de los kaldorei. Hoy en día, sus columnas de piedra blanca y arcos en ruinas están cubiertos de hiedra y helechos silvestres. Situadas al noreste de Satyrnaar y justo al norte del invasivo Aserradero Grito de Guerra, las ruinas ofrecen un mirador tranquilo y estratégico a lo largo de los senderos orientales hacia Azshara y Talloumbrío. Aunque los bosques que la rodean están plagados de corrupción demoníaca e incursiones de la Horda, la ruina en sí conserva una sobrecogedora y sosegada quietud.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The quiet presence of Kayneth Stillwind underscores the Cenarion Circle's solitary vigil in corrupted borderlands, situated right beneath the shadowed canopy near the Great Tree of Bough Shadow.",["faction:Alliance"]="Forest Song serves as a vital solitary outpost for Alliance adventurers cutting across northeastern Ashenvale toward Azshara or Felwood."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Currently, Forest Song is inhabited by the night elf druid Kayneth Stillwind, who stands watch alone amidst the ancient ruins.",["al"]={"who is at forest song","forest song npcs","forest song inhabitants"},["q"]="Who lives at Forest Song?"},{["a"]="The ruins lie perilously close to Satyrnaar to the southwest, crawling with corrupted satyrs, and the Warsong Lumber Camp to the south. To the northeast lies Bough Shadow, where the green dragonflight guards a Great Tree leading into the Emerald Dream.",["al"]={"forest song dangers","enemies near forest song"},["q"]="What threats are near Forest Song?"},{["a"]="Kayneth monitors hostile movements throughout the eastern forests, directing allies against regional dangers—including sinister ventures and diseases spread by the Forsaken operating in the area.",["al"]={"why is kayneth here","kayneth stillwind purpose"},["q"]="Why is Kayneth Stillwind stationed here?"},{["a"]="No. Unlike Astranaar, Forest Song is largely an unfortified ruin without an active garrison, vendors, or military infrastructure, maintained only as a lone forward lookout post.",["al"]={"alliance town forest song","is forest song a town"},["q"]="Is Forest Song a major Alliance settlement?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","bough shadow","eastern ashenvale","forest song","kaldorei ruins","kayneth stillwind","satyrnaar"},["n"]="Forest Song",["s"]="Forest Song is an ancient night elf ruin nestled in northeastern Ashenvale, near the tainted woods of Satyrnaar and the great portal at Bough Shadow. At present, it stands largely deserted save for the vigilant druid Kayneth Stillwind, who watches over the eastern border against emergent threats.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the dense woodlands of northeastern Ashenvale, Forest Song was once an elegant settlement of the kaldorei. Today, white stone columns and crumbling archways are overgrown with ivy and wild ferns. Located northeast of Satyrnaar and just north of the encroaching Warsong Lumber Camp, the ruins hold a quiet, strategic overlook along the eastern trails toward Azshara and Bough Shadow. While the woods around it are plagued by demonic corruption and Horde incursions, the ruin itself maintains a haunting, tranquil stillness.",["t"]="A Lonely Vigil in Eastern Ashenvale"},{["b"]="Forest Song is currently manned solely by the druid Kayneth Stillwind. From this crumbling outpost, Stillwind keeps a watchful eye on the dark designs of enemies entering the wilderness, including the unsettling presence of the Forsaken in the eastern forests. Though isolated far from Astranaar and lacking garrison fortifications, the sanctuary serves as an important rallying point for Alliance travelers venturing toward the northern road into Felwood or investigating the corruptions seeping across the canopy.",["t"]="Watcher of the Border"}}}}}
t["subzone:forlorn-cavern"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,316,25.635.0,49.190.0,39.307.0,59.220.0",["h"]="64cb07",["n"]="Caverna Abandonada",["s"]="Caverna Abandonada. Enclavada a lo largo de la orilla norte del lago subterráneo de Forjaz, Caverna Abandonada es un distrito aislado y tenuemente iluminado, muy alejado de la bulliciosa Gran Fundición de la ciudad. Sirve como un sombrío refugio donde ladrones, carteristas y practicantes de las artes oscuras llevan a cabo sus asuntos lejos de las miradas indiscretas de la guardia enana. Mientras el resto de Forjaz resuena con los golpes de yunque y radia el calor de la Gran Fundición, Caverna Abandonada es fría, húmeda y silenciosa. Siguiendo el borde norte del lago subterráneo de la montaña, sus sinuosos senderos permanecen convenientemente ocultos entre Sala Mística y Sala de los Expedicionarios. Su penumbra la convierte en el lugar de reunión ideal para quienes prefieren mantener sus asuntos con discreción. Las autoridades locales hacen la vista gorda en gran medida, dejando que los carteristas comparen venenos, que los brujos consulten grimorios a puerta cerrada y que los artesanos discretos —como forjadores de armas y pescadores solitarios— ejerzan sus oficios sin ser molestados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The cavern serves as the Alliance's primary rogue hub within Khaz Modan, offering poisons, specialized blades, and discreet trainers hidden along the damp stone walkways.",["class:Warlock"]="Dwarven society vehemently distrusts fel magic, forcing practitioners to gather inside Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms to bind demons and trade grimoires in secret."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The cavern sits in the northern portion of Ironforge along the subterranean lake. You can enter it by heading east out of the Mystic Ward or west along the tunnel from the Hall of Explorers.",["al"]={"forlorn cavern location","how to get to forlorn cavern","where is forlorn cavern"},["q"]="Where is the Forlorn Cavern located in Ironforge?"},{["a"]="Ironforge's civil authorities and clergy take a dim view of both demonic pacts and organized pickpocketing. The cavern's secluded, poorly lit corners provide warlock cabals and the thieves' guild the discretion they need to train novices and trade illicit goods without provoking the mountain king's guards.",["al"]={"why warlocks here","why rogues in forlorn cavern","shady district ironforge"},["q"]="Why do rogues and warlocks gather here?"},{["a"]="Aside from rogue and warlock trainers, the cavern features Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms catering to practitioners of dark magic, the Stoneblade weapon shop, and a quiet angling supply post known as The Traveling Fisherman.",["al"]={"forlorn cavern vendors","shops in forlorn cavern"},["q"]="What shops and services can be found in the Forlorn Cavern?"}},["kw"]={"bonegrip","forlorn cavern","hall of explorers","ironforge lake","mystic ward","rogue trainers","stoneblade","warlock trainers"},["n"]="Forlorn Cavern",["s"]="Tucked along the northern shores of Ironforge's subterranean lake, the Forlorn Cavern is a dimly lit, secluded district far removed from the city's bustling Great Forge. It serves as a shadowy refuge where thieves, cutpurses, and practitioners of the dark arts conduct their business away from prying dwarven guards.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While the rest of Ironforge clangs with anvil strikes and radiates heat from the Great Forge, the Forlorn Cavern is cold, damp, and hushed. Wrapping along the northern edge of the mountain's underground lake, the winding pathways sit comfortably out of sight between the Mystic Ward and the Hall of Explorers. Its gloom makes it an ideal gathering place for those who prefer to keep their affairs discreet. Local authorities largely turn a blind eye, leaving cutpurses to compare poisons, warlocks to consult grimoires behind closed doors, and quiet tradesfolk—like weapon smiths and lone fishermen—to ply their crafts undisturbed.",["t"]="Ironforge's Shaded Corner"}}}}}
t["subzone:forlorn-rowe"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,253,20.441.0,18.396.1,34.140.0,30.158.0,41.184.1,41.141.0",["h"]="c0970d",["n"]="Loma Inhóspita",["s"]="Loma Inhóspita. La Loma Inhóspita es una colina lúgubre y sombría situada en el límite septentrional del Cementerio del Cerro del Cuervo, en el Bosque del Ocaso. Es tristemente célebre por ser la oscura morada de Morbent Vil, un nigromante cuya magia malévola reanima a los muertos inquietos por todo el bosque. Elevándose a lo largo del extremo norte del Cementerio del Cerro del Cuervo, la Loma Inhóspita se halla perpetuamente envuelta en penumbra. En lo alto de esta elevación se encuentra el hogar de Morbent Vil, el nigromante similar a un liche responsable de gran parte de los muertos vivientes que acechan las tierras salvajes circundantes. Atado por viles encantamientos arcanos, el señor de la colina dirige a sus sirvientes esqueléticos desde esta atalaya, haciendo que todo el rincón noroccidental del Bosque del Ocaso sea peligroso para los viajeros.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,1,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="The dark rites woven at the Forlorn Rowe represent an affront to the Holy Light, requiring consecrated relics and righteous wrath to pierce the necromancer's wards.",["faction:Alliance"]="Rooting out Morbent Fel from the Forlorn Rowe is critical for restoring a semblance of safety to Duskwood's western border."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Forlorn Rowe is situated in northwestern Duskwood, resting directly on the northern ridge overlooking the sprawling Raven Hill Cemetery.",["al"]={"forlorn rowe location","where is forlorn rowe","find forlorn rowe"},["q"]="Where is the Forlorn Rowe located?"},{["a"]="It is the lair of Morbent Fel, a powerful and malevolent necromancer who uses dark arcane rites to raise and command the legions of undead wandering Duskwood.",["al"]={"who is at forlorn rowe","forlorn rowe boss","house on the hill duskwood"},["q"]="Who lives at the Forlorn Rowe?"},{["a"]="Morbent Fel shields himself with foul sorcery, rendering mundane attacks almost useless until he is stripped of his dark protections by a consecrated relic crafted to dispel his magic.",["al"]={"morbent fel shield","morbent fel immune","how to kill morbent fel"},["q"]="Why is Morbent Fel so hard to fight here?"},{["a"]="Yes, it stands as an elevated bluff along the northern boundary of the Raven Hill Cemetery, directly overlooking the graves and crypts below.",["al"]={"is forlorn rowe raven hill","raven hill connection"},["q"]="Is the Forlorn Rowe part of the cemetery?"}},["kw"]={"cemetery","duskwood","forlorn rowe","morbent fel","necromancer","raven hill","undead"},["n"]="Forlorn Rowe",["s"]="The Forlorn Rowe is an ominous, shadowy hill perched on the northern boundary of the Raven Hill Cemetery in Duskwood. It is infamous as the dark abode of Morbent Fel, a necromancer whose malevolent magic animates the restless dead throughout the forest.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Rising along the northern edge of the Raven Hill Cemetery, the Forlorn Rowe is perpetually cloaked in gloom. Atop this rise sits the home of Morbent Fel, the lich-like necromancer responsible for much of the walking dead haunting the surrounding wilderness. Bound by foul arcane enchantments, the master of the hill directs his skeletal servants from this vantage, rendering the entire northwestern corner of Duskwood perilous for travelers.",["t"]="A Seat of Necromancy"},{["b"]="Morbent Fel's grasp on the Forlorn Rowe cannot be broken by ordinary steel alone. His dark enchantments protect his physical form from mortal weapons until he is weakened by specialized relics of holy power. Bringing down the necromancer and breaking his hold over the woods requires adventurers to secure consecrated armaments, striking at the heart of the curse smothering the cemetery grounds.",["t"]="Cleansing the Hill"}}}}}
t["subzone:freewind-post"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,279,21.659.0,31.565.1,48.245.0,41.297.0,65.276.0,48.249.0",["h"]="1d59ae",["n"]="Poblado Viento Libre",["s"]="Poblado Viento Libre. El Poblado Viento Libre es el principal puesto de avanzada de la Horda en Las Mil Agujas, encaramado en lo alto de una de las impresionantes mesetas de piedra del cañón. Accesible principalmente mediante un ascensor tauren y serpenteantes puentes de cuerda, sirve como refugio defensivo frente a las partidas de guerra centauro y como un enclave fronterizo vital. Construido directamente sobre las mesetas del cañón, el Poblado Viento Libre confía en el ingenio y la altura para proteger a su gente. Los centauros Galak dominan el árido fondo del cañón que se extiende abajo, pero no pueden escalar con eficacia los imponentes acantilados ni franquear los pesados montacargas de madera que suben a los viajeros de la Horda hacia el cielo. Un laberinto de puentes de cuerdas y tablones conecta Viento Libre con las agujas vecinas, conformando un nido seguro. Más allá de mantener a raya a las partidas de saqueo centauro, el puesto de avanzada también ayuda a controlar a las chillonas arpías que anidan a lo largo de los riscos y atiende los cercanos terrenos de dracoleones en Nido Alto, donde se recolectan huevos salvajes para criarlos como leales monturas de jinete del viento para la Horda.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post is the sole major Horde sanctuary and flight connection between the Southern Barrens and Tanaris, providing essential logistical support across central Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="Freewind Post displays the architectural ingenuity of the shu'halo, adapting mesa heights to shut out traditional centaur marauders while tending the ancestral wyverns of the bluffs."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The vertical layout keeps the settlement safe from the hostile Galak centaur warbands patrolling the canyon bottom. Centaur excel on flat terrain but cannot scale sheer cliff faces or easily breach the mechanical wooden lifts used by the tauren.",["al"]={"why is freewind post in the sky","why mesa","freewind post elevation"},["q"]="Why is Freewind Post built so high up on a mesa?"},{["a"]="Most travelers use the large mechanical wooden lifts stationed at the base of the main mesa. There is also a back route consisting of a precarious series of rope bridges and wooden ramps winding between neighboring rock pillars, though a careless step can mean a lethal plunge to the canyon floor.",["al"]={"how to get up freewind post","freewind post elevator","freewind entrance"},["q"]="How do you get up and down from the post?"},{["a"]="Relations are deeply strained. The Grimtotem occupying Darkcloud Pinnacle northwest of Freewind Post are accused of murders, kidnappings, and unprovoked hostility toward other tauren, leaving the outpost's defenders in a state of quiet vigilance against their neighboring kin.",["al"]={"grimtotem freewind post","darkcloud pinnacle freewind","why are grimtotem bad here"},["q"]="What is the relationship between Freewind Post and the Grimtotem?"},{["a"]="Highperch is an ancestral nesting ground for wild wyverns just across the canyon. The tauren of Freewind Post monitor these beasts and cull eggs from their nests, which are then nurtured and raised to serve as wind rider mounts throughout the Horde.",["al"]={"why highperch","highperch wyverns freewind"},["q"]="What importance does Highperch have to the post?"}},["kw"]={"darkcloud pinnacle","elevator","freewind post","galak","highperch","mesa","tauren","thousand needles","wyverns"},["n"]="Freewind Post",["s"]="Freewind Post is the primary Horde outpost in Thousand Needles, perched high atop one of the canyon's dramatic stone mesas. Accessible primarily by tauren lift and winding rope bridges, it serves as a defensive refuge against centaur warbands and a vital frontier staging ground.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Built directly upon the canyon mesas, Freewind Post relies on ingenuity and height to safeguard its people. The Galak centaur dominate the arid canyon floor below, but they cannot effectively scale the towering cliffs or breach the heavy wooden elevators that haul Horde travelers up into the sky. A labyrinth of rope and plank bridges connects Freewind to neighboring spires, forming a secure aerie. Beyond keeping centaur raiding parties at bay, the outpost also helps manage the screeching harpies nesting along the bluffs and tends to the nearby wyvern grounds at Highperch, where wild eggs are culled and trained as loyal wind rider mounts for the Horde.",["t"]="A Fortress in the Sky"},{["b"]="Despite its impregnable height, Freewind Post faces growing tension with its neighbors to the northwest: the Grimtotem tribe stationed at Darkcloud Pinnacle. Once tolerated as stubborn traditionalists, the Grimtotem under Chieftain Arnak have increasingly turned to violence, kidnapping, and murder. Suspicious rituals and whispers of dark power surround the nearby peaks. The local tauren watch the skies and rope bridges with growing dread, conscious that their most dangerous enemies do not prowl the salt flats below, but sit entrenched across the canyon winds.",["t"]="Shadows from Darkcloud Pinnacle"}}}}}
t["subzone:frostmane-hold"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,338,28.417.0,25.349.0,28.164.0,32.122.0,44.207.0,35.189.0",["h"]="ad488f",["n"]="Poblado Peloescarcha",["s"]="Poblado Peloescarcha. Poblado Peloescarcha es un campamento fortificado y un complejo de cavernas reclamado por los trols de hielo Peloescarcha en el oeste de Dun Morogh. Escondido entre los riscos al sur de Gnomeregan, sirve como base de operaciones central para los asaltantes trols que invaden el territorio enano. La Guardia de Forjaz vigila de cerca el poblado para calibrar la creciente amenaza trol. Esculpido en los gélidos acantilados del oeste de Dun Morogh, Poblado Peloescarcha está formado por toscas estructuras al aire libre y un sinuoso sistema de cuevas. Para la tribu Peloescarcha, funciona como su fortaleza principal, fuertemente custodiada por despellejadores y cazadores de cabezas. Desde aquí, los trols lanzan incursiones hacia los valles circundantes, poniendo a prueba las defensas de asentamientos cercanos como Kharanos y amenazando a los viajeros a lo largo de los pasos de montaña.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="The Frostmane have contested Dun Morogh for centuries, and clearing out Frostmane Hold is a rite of passage for mountaineers seeking to safeguard Ironforge's snowy heartland.",["race:Gnome"]="Nestled just south of Gnomeregan, the hold represents yet another dangerous hostile front bordering the embattled former gnome capital."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The stronghold is occupied by the Frostmane tribe of ice trolls, specifically their hunters, hideskinners, and headhunters, along with their chieftains and raiders.",["al"]={"who is in frostmane hold","frostmane hold mobs","trolls in frostmane hold"},["q"]="Who lives in Frostmane Hold?"},{["a"]="It lies in the western mountains of Dun Morogh, situated south of the industrial ruins of Gnomeregan and west of Kharanos.",["al"]={"frostmane hold location","where is frostmane hold","find frostmane hold"},["q"]="Where is Frostmane Hold located?"},{["a"]="Dwarven leaders in Kharanos fear that the Frostmane are massing in numbers large enough to stage serious raids on settlements, prompting military leaders to send scouts to map the caves and thin their ranks.",["al"]={"why scout frostmane hold","kharanos troll quest"},["q"]="Why are the dwarves interested in this cave?"},{["a"]="No. In the present era, the stronghold belongs firmly to the Frostmane ice trolls. Trogg activity in Dun Morogh remains primarily centered around their own dens and the ruins of Gnomeregan.",["al"]={"troggs frostmane hold","rockjaw frostmane"},["q"]="Are there troggs in Frostmane Hold?"}},["kw"]={"dun morogh","frostmane","frostmane hold","headhunter","hideskinner","ice troll","kharanos","vejrek"},["n"]="Frostmane Hold",["s"]="Frostmane Hold is a fortified encampment and cavern complex claimed by the Frostmane ice trolls in western Dun Morogh. Tucked into the crags south of Gnomeregan, it serves as a central staging ground for troll raiders encroaching on dwarven territory. The Ironforge Guard keeps a close watch on the hold to gauge the growing troll threat.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the freezing cliffs of western Dun Morogh, Frostmane Hold consists of rough outdoor structures and a winding cave system. For the Frostmane tribe, it functions as a primary stronghold, densely guarded by hideskinners and headhunters. From here, the trolls launch raids into the surrounding valleys, testing the defenses of nearby settlements like Kharanos and menacing travelers along the mountain passes.",["t"]="A Troll Bastion in the Snows"},{["b"]="As tensions in Dun Morogh mount, dwarven commanders in Kharanos have grown increasingly concerned about the scale of the Frostmane buildup. Young mountaineers and adventurers are routinely dispatched to scout the interior caverns, map out the defenses, and cull the warbands before the tribe can muster an organized assault against dwarven outposts.",["t"]="A Thorn in Kharanos' Side"}}}}}
t["subzone:frostmane-hovel"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,218,25.313.0,28.167.0,41.227.0,23.139.0",["h"]="c42ef1",["n"]="Cobertizo Peloescarcha",["s"]="Cobertizo Peloescarcha. Cobertizo Peloescarcha es una guarida en una cueva escarpada escondida en los riscos meridionales del Valle de Crestanevada, en Dun Morogh. Sirve como refugio atrincherado para los agresivos troles Peloescarcha que presionan directamente los campos de entrenamiento de los enanos. Excavado en las montañas del sur que flanquean el Valle de Crestanevada, Cobertizo Peloescarcha da cobijo a troles Peloescarcha autóctonos que se niegan a ceder las nieves perpetuas a Forjaz. Operando desde cavernas rudimentarias como esta, los troles organizan continuos ataques contra los campamentos enanos locales e interrumpen las líneas de suministro hacia el valle.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The persistent Frostmane presence right outside Anvilmar highlights how even the heartland of Ironforge must constantly defend itself against local adversaries.",["race:Dwarf"]="For young Bronzebeard recruits training in Coldridge Valley, securing the perimeter against the hostile Frostmane tribe in caves like this is an essential rite of passage."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Frostmane Hovel is a natural cavern in southern Coldridge Valley used as a foul-weather encampment by indigenous Frostmane trolls encroaching on dwarven territory.",["al"]={"frostmane hovel","what is this cave","coldridge troll cave"},["q"]="What is the Frostmane Hovel?"},{["a"]="The Frostmane tribe has inhabited the snowy peaks of Dun Morogh for generations. Bitter rivals of the Bronzebeard dwarves, they constantly push inward from the high ridges to raid supply paths and challenge dwarven settlements.",["al"]={"why trolls here","dun morogh trolls","frostmane presence"},["q"]="Why are there trolls in Coldridge Valley?"},{["a"]="The cave is occupied by raiding Frostmane trolls who use the sheltered crevice to stage incursions across the southern shelf of the valley.",["al"]={"who leads the cave","who lives in frostmane hovel"},["q"]="Who controls this cave?"}},["kw"]={"anvilmar","coldridge valley","dun morogh","frostmane","hovel","trolls"},["n"]="Frostmane Hovel",["s"]="Frostmane Hovel is a rugged cave den tucked into the southern crags of Coldridge Valley in Dun Morogh. It serves as an entrenched shelter for aggressive Frostmane trolls pressing directly into dwarven training grounds.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the southern mountains flanking Coldridge Valley, the Frostmane Hovel shelters indigenous Frostmane trolls who refuse to yield the high snows to Ironforge. Operating out of crude caverns like this, the trolls mount continuous raids against local dwarven camps and disrupt supply lines into the valley.",["t"]="A Troll Den in the Valley"}}}}}
t["subzone:furlbrow-s-pumpkin-farm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="23,278,14.594.0,17.414.0,27.212.0,26.207.0,28.163.0,56.178.0",["h"]="811254",["n"]="Plantación de Calabazas de Cejade",["s"]="Plantación de Calabazas de Cejade. La Plantación de Calabazas de Cejade es una granja tomada en el norte de Páramos de Poniente, junto al camino principal desde el Bosque de Elwynn. En su día fue una próspera parcela cuidada por el Granjero Cejade y su esposa Verna, pero los campos y la granja han sido tomados por la Hermandad Defias y por rondadores gólems de la cosecha. Situada cerca de la frontera norte de Páramos de Poniente, la Plantación de Calabazas de Cejade era conocida en el pasado por producir cosechas abundantes para alimentar al reino. Todo terminó cuando la Hermandad Defias arrasó la campiña. Los forajidos expulsaron de sus tierras al Granjero Cejade y a su esposa Verna, dejando sus campos invadidos por gólems de la cosecha mecánicos programados para atacar a cualquiera que se acerque. Con los edificios de la granja ocupados por bandidos y los campos merodeados por maquinaria renegada, los legítimos propietarios se han visto obligados a acampar al borde del camino, cerca de La Finca de Jansen, lamentando la pérdida de su hogar y su sustento.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The overrun farm stands as a stark indictment of Stormwind's inability to protect its own heartland, leaving loyal tax-paying farmers defenseless against banditry."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The farm belongs to Farmer Furlbrow and his wife, Verna Furlbrow. However, they were forced off their property when outlaws seized the area, driving the couple to take refuge along the road near the Jansen Stead.",["al"]={"who owns furlbrow farm","furlbrow owner","who lives here"},["q"]="Who owns this pumpkin farm?"},{["a"]="The farm was violently taken over by the Defias Brotherhood. They drove off the Furlbrows and stationed thugs in the buildings, using haywire mechanical harvest golems to guard the surrounding pumpkin patch.",["al"]={"why is it abandoned","what happened to the farm","why are bandits here"},["q"]="Why is the farm abandoned?"},{["a"]="Farmer Furlbrow and his wife have taken shelter along the main road just northeast of the farm, close to the Jansen Stead, stranded with their cart and belongings.",["al"]={"where is farmer furlbrow","furlbrow location","find furlbrow"},["q"]="Where are the Furlbrows now?"},{["a"]="The mechanical harvesters once worked the fields, but the Defias Brotherhood reprogrammed or repurposed them into deadly sentries that attack any non-Defias trespassers on sight.",["al"]={"harvest golems","why are golems hostile","who made the golems"},["q"]="Why are mechanical harvest golems attacking people here?"}},["kw"]={"defias","farm","furlbrow","harvest golem","jansen","pumpkin","verna","westfall"},["n"]="Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm",["s"]="Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm is an overrun homestead in northern Westfall, just off the main road from Elwynn Forest. Once a prosperous plot tended by Farmer Furlbrow and his wife Verna, the fields and farmhouse have been seized by the Defias Brotherhood and prowling harvest golems.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated near the northern border of Westfall, Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm was once known for producing robust crops to feed the kingdom. That ended when the Defias Brotherhood swept across the countryside. Outlaws drove Farmer Furlbrow and his wife Verna from their land, leaving their fields overrun with mechanical harvest golems programmed to attack anyone approaching. With the farm buildings occupied by bandits and the fields prowled by renegade machinery, the rightful owners have been forced to camp along the roadside near the Jansen Stead, mourning the loss of their home and livelihood.",["t"]="A Harvest Lost"},{["b"]="The farm's fall illustrates the broader collapse of law and order across Westfall. With Stormwind's military garrison spread thin and unable to safeguard rural freeholders, the Defias Brotherhood easily claimed homesteads like Furlbrow's. Bandits use the property as an staging ground and camp while letting lethal harvest watchers guard the perimeter, leaving travelers on the nearby highway vulnerable to ambush.",["t"]="Defias Stronghold"}}}}}
t["subzone:galardell-valley"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,218,26.483.0,34.167.0,34.139.0,46.128.0,26.213.0",["h"]="d39815",["n"]="Valle de Galardell",["s"]="Valle de Galardell. El Valle de Galardell es un cañón escarpado y peligroso enclavado en las alturas del noreste de las Montañas Crestagrana. El desfiladero está infestado de agresivas manadas de gnomos y se alza bajo la sombra de la infame Torre de Ilgalar. Esculpido en los acantilados del noreste de Crestagrana, el Valle de Galardell ha escapado por completo al control de los defensores de Villa del Lago. Fieros gnomos de Crestagrana merodean por las tierras bajas y acampan a lo largo del fondo del cañón, organizados bajo brutales líderes de manada como el teniente Fangore. Elevándose por encima de los barrancos se encuentra la oscura aguja de la Torre de Ilgalar, el bastión del mago renegado Morganth, lo que convierte a todo el valle en una fuente constante de pavor para los asentamientos cercanos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire's overwhelmed town guard cannot secure the northeast road as long as gnoll packs and Morganth's dark presence hold Galardell Valley."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Galardell Valley is situated in the far northeastern corner of the Redridge Mountains, tucked behind the high crags beyond the roads leading north from Lake Everstill.",["al"]={"galardell valley location","where is galardell valley","how to find galardell valley"},["q"]="Where is Galardell Valley located?"},{["a"]="The valley is overrun by bloodthirsty gnoll packs who patrol the trails in dense clusters, led by dangerous brutes like Lieutenant Fangore.",["al"]={"mobs in galardell valley","who lives in galardell valley","galardell enemies"},["q"]="What creatures live in the valley?"},{["a"]="That is the Tower of Ilgalar, an imposing stone structure that serves as the base of operations for the rogue sorcerer Morganth.",["al"]={"galardell valley tower","spire above galardell","tower near gnolls redridge"},["q"]="What is the dark tower overlooking the valley?"},{["a"]="Lieutenant Fangore is a formidable gnoll leader stationed within the valley. Known for his cunning and ferocity, he will howl for aid from nearby gnoll packs when challenged, quickly overwhelming unwary travelers.",["al"]={"fangore","lieutenant fangore","galardell valley boss"},["q"]="Who is Lieutenant Fangore?"}},["kw"]={"fangore","galardell valley","gnolls","morganth","redridge","tower of ilgalar"},["n"]="Galardell Valley",["s"]="Galardell Valley is a rugged, dangerous canyon nestled in the northeastern heights of the Redridge Mountains. The gorge is overrun by aggressive gnoll packs and sits beneath the shadow of the infamous Tower of Ilgalar.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the northeastern cliffs of Redridge, Galardell Valley has fallen completely out of the control of Lakeshire's defenders. Fierce Redridge gnolls prowl the lowlands and camp along the canyon floor, organized under brutal pack leaders such as Lieutenant Fangore. Towering high above the ravines stands the dark spire of the Tower of Ilgalar, the stronghold of the renegade mage Morganth, making the entire valley a persistent source of dread for the surrounding settlements.",["t"]="A Den of Beasts and Shadow"}}}}}
t["subzone:gallows-end-tavern"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,258,30.446.0,21.405.0,41.114.0,40.248.0,34.165.0,45.170.0",["h"]="7f646b",["n"]="Mesón La Horca",["s"]="Mesón La Horca. El Mesón La Horca es la posada principal de Rémol y el corazón de la hospitalidad de los Renegados en los Claros de Tirisfal. Más allá de ofrecer cobijo y licores a los viajeros agotados, sirve como un centro esencial para mentores de clase, instructores de profesión e interrogatorios encubiertos. Erigido de forma prominente junto al camino en Rémol, el Mesón La Horca sirve como el principal punto de encuentro para los Renegados recién despertados que parten de Camposanto y viajan hacia el sur, rumbo a Entrañas. A pesar de su condición de no-muertos, los Renegados siguen frecuentando sus salas en busca de camaradería, comercio y refugio. La posada alberga a varios instructores de clase —que guían a jóvenes guerreros, sacerdotes, magos, pícaros y brujos—, así como a vendedores y profesionales de la medicina.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Beneath the taproom floors, the Forsaken keep captured Alliance scouts and Scarlet Crusade zealots detained for intelligence and interrogation.",["race:Undead"]="As the first major inn encountered outside Deathknell, Gallows' End Tavern serves as the cultural and functional crossroads for newly awakened Forsaken entering the wider world."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is located in the center of Brill, the main Forsaken settlement just north of the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"gallows end location","where is gallows end tavern","brill inn location"},["q"]="Where is the Gallows' End Tavern located?"},{["a"]="While the Forsaken do not require sleep or mortal sustenance to survive, taverns like Gallows' End maintain social bonds and cultural habits from their past lives. It also acts as a secure civic center for training, commerce, and official business.",["al"]={"why do undead drink","why do forsaken need taverns","undead inn lore"},["q"]="Why do the undead need an inn or tavern?"},{["a"]="In the cellars beneath the tavern, the Forsaken hold captive enemies including a Scarlet Zealot from the hostile Scarlet Crusade and an Alliance Dwarven Mountaineer.",["al"]={"tavern prisoners","who is in the cellar","brill tavern dungeon"},["q"]="Who is imprisoned in the basement?"},{["a"]="The tavern features instructors for warriors, priests, mages, rogues, and warlocks, along with first aid and enchanting trainers, general trade vendors, and an innkeeper.",["al"]={"gallows end trainers","who trains in brill inn","tavern vendors"},["q"]="What services and trainers can be found here?"}},["kw"]={"brill","forsaken","gallows end","gallows' end tavern","innkeeper","scarlet zealot","tirisfal glades","undead"},["n"]="Gallows' End Tavern",["s"]="Gallows' End Tavern is the principal inn of Brill and the heart of Forsaken hospitality in Tirisfal Glades. Beyond offering shelter and spirits to weary travelers, it serves as an essential hub for class mentors, trade instructors, and covert interrogations.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing prominently along the road in Brill, Gallows' End Tavern serves as the primary gathering place for newly awakened Forsaken leaving Deathknell and journeying south toward the Undercity. Despite their undead condition, Forsaken still frequent its halls for fellowship, trade, and refuge. The inn houses various class instructors—guiding young warriors, priests, mages, rogues, and warlocks—as well as vendors and medical practitioners.",["t"]="A Gathering Place for the Dead"},{["b"]="Beneath the creaking floorboards and tavern laughter lies a far grimmer purpose. Down in the cellars, the Forsaken keep prisoners of war bound and guarded away from public view. Among them are a captured Scarlet Zealot and a Dwarven Mountaineer, held beneath the tavern for interrogation and experimentation as the Forsaken fight to secure their borders against both zealous crusaders and Alliance scouts.",["t"]="Secrets in the Cellar"}}}}}
